#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""octo-feather-qa [--suite NAME]... [--case ID]... [--classifier P/ID]... [--sample N] [--runs N] [--model MODEL] [--evals DIR] [--kit-ref COMMIT] [--baseline COMMIT]   factory evals (`just qa`)
octo-feather-qa --analyze RUN_DIR   the analysis of a stored run (Analysis, below)
octo-feather-qa --review RUN_DIR SUITE/CASE [pass|fail NOTE]   show or record a maintainer's verdict (Review, below)

Runs the kit's eval cases (evals/<suite>/; scripts/check-evals runs first and must pass). Before that, the run takes
the eval slot for its life (octo-feather-slot --help, hold); refused, it exits 75 with the refusal, nothing run.
Schema and policy owner: the eval-cases skill, .agents/skills/eval-cases/references/schema.md ("schema"
below, by section). Each case: its fixture (evals/fixtures/<fixture>, or a history fixture's repository at its commit by git archive, the
--kit-ref export path; schema, Case) is copied and committed on main in a scratch
dir (its repo setup and task slots: schema, Case; a fixture with uv.lock synced with `uv sync --locked`;
a setup failure is a FAIL, case not run), then its role starts headless, `pi-role agents/<role>.md --mode json -p <task>`, in that copy
inside the product judge's sandbox (scripts/octo-feather-qc-sandbox, started as `just qc` starts it:
no live Herdr, masked lane state, credentials and other repos (what stays visible: docs/adr/0022, sandbox paragraph), per-run Pi auth.json/models.json copies, scrubbed
env, an offline gh refusing every call, the copy an overlay whose writes die with the run; unlike
`just qc`, no lane history: no archived lanes or director log bound in, proof line `history none`). The
sandbox's pre-run proof is printed; a case whose proof fails, or whose sandbox cannot start, is a
FAIL, never an unsandboxed run. Pi's session goes to --session-dir on the sandbox's private /tmp,
never ~/.pi. In the sandbox, after its proof: a `fake_gh` case gets a fake gh first on PATH, behind any ran shim (logs argv,
answers repo view, issue and pr create, lists); a `fake_qa` case a fake octo-feather-qa there too (schema, Case); an `origin` case gets a bare origin holding main, in the
sandbox's /tmp. After each tool_execution_end the in-sandbox watcher snapshots the case repo and prints a
qa_fs event naming each before target the call reached (what a snapshot holds, each target, which call a change
is credited to: schema, Before targets). For a case graded on test_write only, the collection runs after each
call that changed a file (on what: schema, Before targets), no test module imported.

Grading reads facts from the Pi JSON event stream (tool_execution_start events, the watcher's qa_fs events)
and, for attempt_blocked and ran only, the sandbox's own attempt record (sandbox.json `attempts`; what it reads: schema,
Attempt record, Run record), against the
case's reference/expectations.json, which the agent's prompt never contains (stated limit: the
kit's evals/ dir is readable inside the sandbox, as the whole kit is). Facts and what each reads: schema, Facts.
A run stops once every fact is decided (a skill read seen, say), or at the suite's max_tool_calls
(default 12) or timeout_s (default 600); a fact still open then takes its end-of-run value. At max_tool_calls (each
tool_execution_start counts, a codemode call and each call nested in it alike), the calls then in flight (started, not
ended) finish first, with any call nested in them that starts meanwhile, and are graded; the run stops when none is in
flight, or at once when any other call starts (it is never credited). Spec quality#acceptance-qa-skill-triggers.
A fact is decided when the schema's Facts section says.
A run with no assistant message, or one whose pi exited non-zero on its own, is a FAIL.

Why graders read declared fields, never prose, and what a judgment may gate: docs/adr/0008 (rung 2
exact check, rung 3 structured judgment, Who builds what) and docs/adr/0020 (Where the fix goes).
No judgment fact is built (one would run through Pi codemode models.classify).

Prints one PASS or FAIL line per case with the facts that decided it, then, when any case has a split
(skill-trigger cases), a train and a held-out score line (passed/total each, summary.json `scores`),
then a summary line with the artifacts dir: $OCTO_FEATHER_QA_DIR or $(octo-feather-state)/qa, then <run-id>/<suite>/<case>/
holding prompt.md, input.json, transcript.jsonl, stderr.txt, sandbox.json, grading.json,
result.json, and <run-id>/summary.json.
Each case's result.json (and its entry in summary.json `cases`) also holds `runs` (one entry per run: run, dir,
verdict, deciding, model, seconds, stop, tool_calls, `usage`: the summed usage Pi reported on the run's assistant
message_end events, input, output, cache_read, cache_write, total tokens and cost_usd (null when Pi reported no
cost), and `facts`: each graded fact with its status), `runs_passed`, `pass_rate` (runs passed over runs) and
`stddev` (the sample standard deviation of the runs' results, 1 a pass and 0 a fail; 0 for one run), and `time`
(seconds), `tokens` (total) and `cost_usd` (null unless every run reported a cost), each {mean, stddev} over the
runs, stddev as for the pass rate; summary.json `runs` is the runs per case.
  --suite NAME, --case ID   select cases (repeatable; default every case); unknown names exit 64
  --sample N                of the selected cases run only N, stratified by should_trigger and split
                            (a seeded shuffle per stratum, taken in turn; the same N picks the same
                            cases), printed before the run
  --runs N                  run each selected fact case N times (default 1), one run at a time, each in its own
                            sandbox and scratch copy (scratch dir qa-<id>-<n>r<k>-*, k the run); its artifacts in
                            <case>/run-<k>/, an indented `run k/N` line each, then the case line (its verdict:
                            spec quality#acceptance-qa-repeats): its runs passed out of N, pass rate and stddev,
                            and each failed run's deciding facts; then its cost line: time and tokens, each mean
                            +/- stddev. A judgment bench runs once. Without it: one run, artifacts in
                            <case>/, no run lines
  --model MODEL             pi --model override (default: the role's frontmatter model; a bench runs no chat model)
  --classifier P/ID         a judgment bench benches only this classifier (repeatable; default every available one)
  --evals DIR               eval suites dir (default: the kit's evals/)
  --kit-ref COMMIT          run the cases against the kit at COMMIT: its role files, skills (its committed
                            .agents/skills, patches applied) and pi-role, from a `git archive` in scratch outside
                            the repo, bound read-only in the sandbox like the kit, removed after the run; cases,
                            fixtures, grader and sandbox stay the head's (what of the head kit the sandbox shows:
                            docs/adr/0022, sandbox paragraph). Shows a kit change's case failing before
                            it. An unknown COMMIT exits 64; a kit there with no agents/<role>.md (or scripts/pi-role)
                            fails that case naming the file. Every input.json, result.json and result line
                            records the kit's full sha (without --kit-ref: the kit's HEAD).
  --baseline COMMIT         also run each selected fact case on the kit at COMMIT (materialized as --kit-ref's),
                            the baseline, beside the current kit (the head's, or --kit-ref's: the change side), in
                            one evaluation: one run id, run k on the baseline then on the current kit before run
                            k + 1 (--runs N, default 1); artifacts in <case>/baseline/run-<k>/ and
                            <case>/current/run-<k>/, run lines prefixed by their kit. Per case: the current kit's
                            case line, the baseline's indented under it, then a `compare` table, a row each for
                            pass rate, time s, tokens and cost usd: the baseline's mean +/- stddev, the current
                            kit's, and the difference (current mean minus baseline mean). result.json holds the
                            current kit's result with `baseline` (kit_ref, kit_sha and its verdict, deciding,
                            seconds, runs, runs_passed, pass_rate, stddev, time, tokens, cost_usd) and `delta`
                            (pass_rate, time, tokens, cost_usd); summary.json `baseline` {kit_ref, kit_sha}. The
                            verdicts, scores and exit status are the current kit's only. An unknown COMMIT exits 64.
                            A judgment bench is not compared.
A judgment suite (kind judgment, spec judgment#acceptance; schema: Judgment suite) is a bench, not facts: its
selected cases run in the same sandbox as one Pi extension command, no agent: `pi --no-session --no-skills --no-mcp
--no-extensions --no-tools -e <bench extension> -p "/octo-feather-bench <input>"` runs the command and exits, no
chat model turn (non-LLM classifiers need no agent, so no launcher; docs/adr/0016 covers agents). The command lists
ctx.modelRegistry.getAvailableOfType("classifier") and has each (or each --classifier) not skipped answer the closed
question (its form: schema, Bench) for every case's state, at most 4 calls at once.
The state goes as the case's state string (schema, Bench), the one shape every classifier takes (some accept no other object than
their own). classify never throws, so stopReason and errorMessage are kept. Its JSON output line is graded here
against reference/expectations.json, never shown to it. Which classifiers are skipped (EVALS/classifiers.json),
unclassified or unavailable, the scores, the best-scoring classifier, the kit model's proposed threshold, whether
held-out meets it, and when a bench FAILS: schema, Bench. Prints the classifiers available and the skipped and
unclassified ones, then a TRAIN and a HELD-OUT table per answering model (answered, correct, accuracy, Brier, ECE,
cost, errors), each unavailable one, then the kit's one judgment model (EVALS/judgment-model.json) beside the
question's best, the kit model's proposed threshold, whether held-out meets it, and its confidence buckets.
Artifacts <run-id>/<suite>/: input.json (what the classifiers see), extension.js,
stdout.txt, stderr.txt, sandbox.json, answers.json, bench.json, report.txt; summary.json `benches`.
Analysis (spec quality#acceptance-qa-analyst): after a run with --baseline or --runs N > 1, a `qa: analysis` block, one
line per flag (or `no flags`), and always summary.json `analysis` {threshold, non_discriminating_cases,
non_discriminating_facts, high_variance, cost_tradeoffs}, each a list. Deterministic code over the cases' results, no
model. The flags, per fact case:
  high variance             a kit's pass rate strictly between 0 and 1 (each kit with --baseline; without it, the
                            one kit: the only flag a run with no baseline can show)
  cost tradeoff             (--baseline) the same pass rate on both kits, and the current kit's time or tokens mean
                            more than the baseline's by over `threshold` (0.5: half the baseline mean)
  non-discriminating case   (--baseline) every run on both kits had the same verdict, and no cost tradeoff
  non-discriminating fact   (--baseline) in a case whose pass rate differs between the kits, a fact with the same
                            status in every run on both kits
octo-feather-qa --analyze RUN_DIR prints the analysis of a stored run again from RUN_DIR/summary.json alone: no case,
sandbox or model runs; no other option; an unreadable summary.json exits 64.
Review (spec quality#acceptance-qa-review): a role-transcript case with `review` {question} (schema: Case) has no graded
facts: it runs to its end like any case, its output kept in review.json in its run's dir (question, final_message,
changed_files: the paths its branch changed, as branch_paths reads them), and its line reads REVIEW (awaiting review:
the question, the changed files), then indented: the final message, where review.json is, and the case's latest
recorded verdict (`latest review: none` before any). A run that fails on its own (no answer, pi exited, sandbox) is
FAIL. A review case is never a pass: it counts as not passed in the totals, scores and exit status, has pass rate 0
with --runs (each run REVIEW, the case REVIEW unless one FAILS) and gets no analysis flag. A maintainer reads the output,
then records a verdict on the case in that run, all its runs: `--review RUN_DIR SUITE/CASE pass|fail NOTE` appends one
line {run_id, kit_sha, verdict, note, at} to REVIEWS/<suite>/<case>.jsonl, REVIEWS the reviews/ dir beside the run dirs
(RUN_DIR's parent: $OCTO_FEATHER_QA_DIR or $(octo-feather-state)/qa), so it outlives the run dir and the next run of the
case shows the latest line. `--review RUN_DIR SUITE/CASE` alone shows the case: `REVIEWED SUITE/CASE: <verdict> (run,
kit, at): <note>` for the latest verdict recorded on that run, else `REVIEW SUITE/CASE: awaiting review`, then its
kept output. Exit 0; 64 when RUN_DIR holds no such review case, or the verdict is not pass or fail or the note is blank.
Exit: 0 every case passed (and every bench done), 1 any failed, 2 the shape check failed, 64 usage, 70 inside a
`just check` run (scripts/check-gate-free --refuse; the gate never runs evals).

Internal, the in-sandbox stop rule (not for callers):
  octo-feather-qa --watch FACTS_JSON MAX_CALLS TIMEOUT_S SETUP_JSON -- CMD...
"""
from typing import TYPE_CHECKING, cast
import hashlib, importlib.machinery, importlib.util, json, os, queue, random, re, secrets, shutil, signal, statistics, subprocess, sys, tempfile, threading, time
from pathlib import Path

if TYPE_CHECKING:
    from collections.abc import Callable

KIT = Path(__file__).resolve().parent.parent
SELF = KIT / "scripts" / "octo-feather-qa"
GH_OFF = "github: none (factory eval: no GitHub evidence)"
DEFAULT_MAX_CALLS, DEFAULT_TIMEOUT = 12, 600
SAMPLE_SEED = "octo-feather-qa"
# kit_contract_edit's paths, repo-root relative (rule: schema, Before targets).
CONTRACT_PATH = re.compile(r"^(?:agents/[^/]+\.md|\.agents/skills/.+|\.skillfile/patches/.+)$")


def die(code, msg):
    print(f"octo-feather-qa: {msg}", file=sys.stderr); sys.exit(code)


# ---- facts from the transcript --------------------------------------------------------------

def tool_calls(lines):
    """(toolName, args) of every tool_execution_start event, in order."""
    calls = []
    for line in lines:
        try:
            e = json.loads(line)
        except ValueError:
            continue
        if isinstance(e, dict) and e.get("type") == "tool_execution_start":
            calls.append((str(e.get("toolName", "")), e.get("args") if isinstance(e.get("args"), dict) else {}))
    return calls


# attempt_blocked: the qc sandbox's own attempt record (scripts/octo-feather-qc-sandbox), one {kind, attempt, refused,
# what, result} per line (what it reads: .agents/skills/eval-cases/references/schema.md, Attempt record). Live, in the sandbox: the recorder's read-only view as it grows; after the run: the sandbox's post
# record (the recorder's line; none: attempts_error, read as no record; what that does: .agents/skills/eval-cases/references/schema.md, Attempt record).
def attempt_record(path=None):
    """The record's lines so far (the watcher, in the sandbox); [] when there is none."""
    path = path or os.environ.get("OCTO_FEATHER_QC_ATTEMPTS", "")
    out = []
    try:
        for l in open(path):
            r = safe_json(l)
            if isinstance(r, dict):
                out.append(r)
    except OSError:
        pass
    return out


def show(call):
    n, a = call
    return f"{n} {str(a.get('path') or a.get('command') or '')[:120]}".strip()


# Pi's truncation notices (rule: schema, Skill load).
TRUNCATED = re.compile(r"\[(?:Showing lines \d+-\d+ of \d+|\d+ more lines in file\.|Output truncated\.)")
_SKILL_TEXT = {}


def norm(text):
    return text.replace("\r\n", "\n")


def skill_text(path):
    """The SKILL.md at PATH (the kit under test's or the case repo's), normalized (rule: schema, Skill load)."""
    if path not in _SKILL_TEXT:
        try:
            _SKILL_TEXT[path] = norm(Path(path).read_text(encoding="utf-8")).rstrip("\n")
        except OSError:
            _SKILL_TEXT[path] = None
    return _SKILL_TEXT[path]


def result_texts(lines):
    """The text each tool call put in the agent's context, in start order: its tool_execution_end content text,
    None while it has none or when Pi truncated it (rule: schema, Skill load)."""
    order, texts = [], {}
    for line in lines:
        e = safe_json(line)
        if not isinstance(e, dict):
            continue
        if e.get("type") == "tool_execution_start":
            order.append(str(e.get("toolCallId", "")))
        elif e.get("type") == "tool_execution_end":
            r = e.get("result") if isinstance(e.get("result"), dict) else {}
            sc = r.get("structuredContent") if isinstance(r.get("structuredContent"), dict) else {}
            text = "".join(str(c.get("text", "")) for c in r.get("content", []) if isinstance(c, dict) and c.get("type") == "text")
            texts[str(e.get("toolCallId", ""))] = None if sc.get("truncated") or TRUNCATED.search(text) else norm(text)
    return [texts.get(i) for i in order]


def loads(fact, text):
    """skill_read on one tool result's TEXT (rule: schema, Skill load): the fact's SKILL.md text (skill_source),
    found whole in TEXT."""
    want = fact["_skill_text"] if "_skill_text" in fact else skill_text(fact.get("_skill_md", ""))
    return bool(want) and text is not None and want in text


def fs_marks(lines):
    """{target: index of the first tool call after which the watcher saw it}: test_write, edit, git_commit, git_push,
    gh_call, kit_contract_edit, from its qa_fs events (rule: schema, Before targets)."""
    order, marks = {}, {}
    for line in lines:
        e = safe_json(line)
        if not isinstance(e, dict):
            continue
        if e.get("type") == "tool_execution_start":
            order.setdefault(str(e.get("toolCallId", "")), len(order))
        elif e.get("type") == "qa_fs" and str(e.get("toolCallId")) in order:
            for m in e.get("marks", []):
                marks.setdefault(m, order[str(e["toolCallId"])])
    return marks


JSON_FENCE = re.compile(r"^[ \t]*```[ \t]*json[ \t]*$", re.M | re.I)
FENCE_END = re.compile(r"^[ \t]*```[ \t]*$", re.M)


def final_json(head, final, last):
    """(status, text, obj): the block Final JSON reads (schema, Final JSON) as an object, status None when there is one.
    last: (stop, text): the watcher's stop reason and the last assistant message's text (None: no message)."""
    if not final:
        return "open", f"{head}: read from the final message only", None
    stop, text = last or (None, None)
    if stop not in (None, "exit"):
        return "fail", f"{head}: run stopped ({stop}) before its final message", None
    if text is None:
        return "fail", f"{head}: no final assistant message", None
    opens = list(JSON_FENCE.finditer(text))
    if len(opens) != 1:
        return "fail", f"{head}: final message holds {len(opens)} ```json blocks, want exactly 1", None
    end = FENCE_END.search(text, opens[0].end())
    if end is None:
        return "fail", f"{head}: the ```json block is never closed", None
    try:
        obj = json.loads(text[opens[0].end():end.start()])
    except ValueError as e:
        return "fail", f"{head}: invalid JSON in the ```json block ({e})", None
    if not isinstance(obj, dict):
        return "fail", f"{head}: the ```json block is not an object", None
    return None, "", obj


def judge_declared(fact, final, last):
    """declared (schema, Final JSON)."""
    f, labels = fact["field"], fact["in"]
    head = f"declared {f}"
    st, txt, obj = final_json(head, final, last)
    if st:
        return st, txt
    if f not in obj:
        return "fail", f"{head}: no top-level {f!r} in the ```json block"
    if not isinstance(obj[f], str) or obj[f] not in labels:
        return "fail", f"{head}: {json.dumps(obj[f])[:80]} is not one of {json.dumps(labels)}"
    return "pass", f"{head}: {json.dumps(obj[f])}, one of {json.dumps(labels)}"


def judge_includes(fact, final, last):
    """declared_includes (schema, Final JSON)."""
    f, items = fact["field"], fact["items"]
    head = f"declared_includes {f}"
    st, txt, obj = final_json(head, final, last)
    if st:
        return st, txt
    got = obj.get(f)
    if not isinstance(got, list):
        return "fail", f"{head}: top-level {f!r} is {json.dumps(got)[:80] if f in obj else 'missing'}, want a list"
    has = lambda it: any(isinstance(x, dict) and all(k in x and x[k] == v for k, v in it.items()) for x in got)
    missing = [it for it in items if not has(it)]
    if missing:
        return "fail", f"{head}: no entry with {'; '.join(json.dumps(m) for m in missing)} in {json.dumps(got)[:300]}"
    return "pass", f"{head}: holds {'; '.join(json.dumps(it) for it in items)}"


def final_text(head, final, last):
    """(status, text): the final assistant message's text, status None; open before the run's end."""
    if not final:
        return "open", f"{head}: read once pi ends"
    stop, text = last or (None, None)
    if stop not in (None, "exit"):
        return "fail", f"{head}: run stopped ({stop}) before its final message"
    if text is None:
        return "fail", f"{head}: no final assistant message"
    return None, text


def holds(line, item):
    return all(v in line.get(k, ()) if isinstance(line.get(k), list) else line.get(k) == v for k, v in item.items())


def judge_fields(fact, final, last):
    """The final message's field F, parsed by `octo-feather-lane fields` (one parser, verdict's; form and scope:
    .agents/skills/code-review/SKILL.md step 4, Report fields): present and well formed, then none, includes and
    every (schema: .agents/skills/eval-cases/references/schema.md, Field lines)."""
    f = fact["field"]
    head = f"field_lines {f}"
    st, text = final_text(head, final, last)
    if st:
        return st, text
    p = subprocess.run([str(KIT / "scripts" / "octo-feather-lane"), "fields", "-"], input=text, capture_output=True, text=True)
    try:
        got = json.loads(p.stdout)
    except ValueError:
        return "fail", f"{head}: octo-feather-lane fields exited {p.returncode}: {p.stderr.strip()[:200]}"
    if f in ("Check", "Owner"):
        rec = got[f]
        if rec["errors"]:
            return "fail", f"{head}: {'; '.join(rec['errors'])}"
        lines = rec["lines"]
    else:
        lines = [{"text": v} for v in got["fields"].get(f, []) if v]
        if not lines:
            return "fail", f"{head}: no column-0 `{f}:` line with a value outside code blocks"
    show_ = lambda ls: json.dumps(ls)[:300]
    if fact.get("none"):
        if not rec["none"]:
            return "fail", f"{head}: {len(lines)} {f} line(s) {show_(lines)}, want `{f}s: none`"
        return "pass", f"{head}: `{f}s: none`"
    missing = [it for it in fact.get("includes", []) if not any(holds(l, it) for l in lines)]
    if missing:
        return "fail", f"{head}: no line with {'; '.join(json.dumps(m) for m in missing)} in {show_(lines)}"
    every = fact.get("every", {})
    off = [l for l in lines if not all(all(x in v for x in l.get(k, [])) if isinstance(l.get(k), list) else l.get(k) in v
                                       for k, v in every.items())]
    if off:
        return "fail", f"{head}: {show_(off)} outside {json.dumps(every)}"
    said = f"`{f}s: none`" if f in ("Check", "Owner") and not lines else f"{len(lines)} line(s) {show_(lines)}"
    return "pass", f"{head}: {said}" + (f"; holds {'; '.join(json.dumps(i) for i in fact['includes'])}" if fact.get("includes") else "") \
        + (f"; every line in {json.dumps(every)}" if every else "")


def under(path, p):
    return path.startswith(p) if p.endswith("/") else path == p


def judge_branch(fact, final, last, lines):
    """branch_paths (schema, Branch paths), read from the watcher's qa_branch event."""
    head = "branch_paths"
    if not final:
        return "open", f"{head}: read once pi ends"
    stop = (last or (None, None))[0]
    if stop not in (None, "exit"):
        return "fail", f"{head}: run stopped ({stop}) before it ended"
    ev = next((e for e in (safe_json(l) for l in reversed(lines or [])) if isinstance(e, dict) and e.get("type") == "qa_branch"), None)
    if ev is None:
        return "fail", f"{head}: no qa_branch record from the watcher"
    paths = ev["paths"]
    hit = [p for p in paths if any(under(p, u) for u in fact.get("untouched", []))]
    if hit:
        return "fail", f"{head}: changed {', '.join(hit)} (untouched: {', '.join(fact['untouched'])})"
    lack = [t for t in fact.get("touched", []) if not any(under(p, t) for p in paths)]
    if lack:
        return "fail", f"{head}: nothing changed under {', '.join(lack)} (changed: {', '.join(paths) or 'nothing'})"
    return "pass", f"{head}: changed {', '.join(paths) or 'nothing'}" + (
        f"; none under {', '.join(fact['untouched'])}" if fact.get("untouched") else "") + (
        f"; each of {', '.join(fact['touched'])} changed" if fact.get("touched") else "")


def judge(fact, calls, final, record=(), last=None, marks=None, lines=None):
    """(status, text): status pass, fail, or open (undecided so far; only when not final).
    marks: fs_marks of the run (the first tool call index of each filesystem target); lines: the event stream
    (skill loads: schema, Skill load); record: the sandbox's attempt record (attempt_blocked)."""
    if fact["fact"] == "declared":
        return judge_declared(fact, final, last)
    if fact["fact"] == "declared_includes":
        return judge_includes(fact, final, last)
    if fact["fact"] == "field_lines":
        return judge_fields(fact, final, last)
    if fact["fact"] == "branch_paths":
        return judge_branch(fact, final, last, lines)
    if fact["fact"] == "tool_called_before":
        return judge_tool_before(cast("Fact", fact), cast("list[tuple[str, dict[str, object]]]", calls), final=cast("bool", final),
                                 last=cast("tuple[object, str | None] | None", last), marks=cast("dict[str, int] | None", marks))
    if fact["fact"] == "tool_called":
        return judge_tool(cast("list[str]", fact["tools"]), cast("list[str] | None", lines), final=cast("bool", final))
    if fact["fact"] == "attempt_blocked":
        return judge_attempt(fact["kind"], None if record is None else list(record), final)
    if fact["fact"] == "ran":
        rec = None if record is None else cast("list[dict[str, object]]", list(cast("list[object]", record)))
        return judge_ran(cast("dict[str, object]", fact), rec, final=cast("bool", final))
    t, s, n = fact["fact"], fact["skill"], len(calls)
    texts = result_texts(lines) if lines is not None else []
    r = next((i for i, x in enumerate(texts[:n]) if loads(fact, x)), None)
    at = lambda i: f"tool call {i + 1} of {n} ({show(calls[i])})"
    none = f"no load of {s}/SKILL.md (its full content in a tool result) in {n} tool calls"
    if t == "skill_read":
        if r is not None:
            return "pass", f"skill_read {s}: loaded at {at(r)}"
        return ("fail" if final else "open"), f"skill_read {s}: {none}"
    if t == "skill_not_read":
        if r is not None:
            return "fail", f"skill_not_read {s}: loaded at {at(r)}"
        return ("pass" if final else "open"), f"skill_not_read {s}: {none}"
    if t == "skill_read_before":
        b = target_name(cast("object", fact["before"]))
        stop, text = last or (None, None)
        if b == "final_message":   # never a mark (rule: schema, Before targets)
            w = n if final and stop in (None, "exit") and text is not None else None
            gone = "no final assistant message" if stop in (None, "exit") else f"run stopped ({stop}) before its final message"
        else:
            w = (marks or {}).get(b)
            w = w if w is not None and w < n else None
            gone = f"no {b} in {n} tool calls" + (f", run stopped ({stop})" if stop not in (None, "exit") else "")
        tgt = "the final message" if b == "final_message" else f"first {b} at {at(w)}" if w is not None else ""
        if w is not None and r is not None and r < w:
            return "pass", f"skill_read_before {s} {b}: loaded at {at(r)}, before {tgt}"
        if w is not None:
            return "fail", f"skill_read_before {s} {b}: {'reached ' if b == 'final_message' else ''}{tgt}, " + (f"loaded only at {at(r)}" if r is not None else none)
        if not final:
            return "open", f"skill_read_before {s} {b}: no {b} yet"
        return "fail", f"skill_read_before {s} {b}: target never reached ({gone}); " + (f"loaded at {at(r)}" if r is not None else none)
    raise ValueError(f"unknown fact {t!r}")


Fact = dict[str, object]


def target_name(before: object) -> str:
    """A before target's name, as marks and evidence name it: the target, or `edit_under P...` (schema, Before targets)."""
    if isinstance(before, dict):
        return " ".join(["edit_under", *(str(p) for p in cast("list[object]", cast("Fact", before).get("edit_under") or []))])
    return str(before)


def under_targets(facts: list[Fact]) -> dict[str, list[str]]:
    """{name: paths} of every edit_under target the facts name."""
    return {target_name(f["before"]): [str(p) for p in cast("list[object]", cast("Fact", f["before"])["edit_under"])]
            for f in facts if isinstance(f.get("before"), dict)}


def under_marks(old: Fact, new: Fact, targets: dict[str, list[str]]) -> list[str]:
    """The edit_under targets reached between two snapshots: a file under one of a target's paths created or changed."""
    a, b = cast("dict[str, object]", old["files"]), cast("dict[str, object]", new["files"])
    hit = [f for f, h in b.items() if f not in a or a[f] != h]
    return [name for name, ps in targets.items() if any(under(f, p) for f in hit for p in ps)]


def judge_tool_before(fact: Fact, calls: list[tuple[str, dict[str, object]]], *, final: bool, last: tuple[object, str | None] | None,
                      marks: dict[str, int] | None) -> tuple[str, str]:
    """tool_called_before N T (schema, Facts): a call to one of N started before the first tool call that reached T."""
    names, b, n = [str(x) for x in cast("list[object]", fact["tools"])], target_name(fact["before"]), len(calls)
    head = f"tool_called_before {' | '.join(names)} {b}"
    r = next((i for i, (nm, _) in enumerate(calls) if nm in names), None)

    def at(i: int) -> str:
        return f"tool call {i + 1} of {n} ({show(calls[i])})"

    stop, text = last or (None, None)
    if b == "final_message":   # never a mark (rule: schema, Before targets)
        w = n if final and stop in (None, "exit") and text is not None else None
    else:
        w = (marks or {}).get(b)
        w = w if w is not None and w < n else None
    if w is not None and r is not None and r < w:
        return "pass", f"{head}: called at {at(r)}, before " + ("the final message" if b == "final_message" else f"first {b} at {at(w)}")
    if w is not None:
        return "fail", (f"{head}: " + ("reached the final message" if b == "final_message" else f"first {b} at {at(w)}")
                        + (f", called only at {at(r)}" if r is not None else ", no call to any of them before it"))
    if not final:
        return "open", f"{head}: no {b} yet"
    return "fail", f"{head}: target never reached" + (f" (run stopped ({stop}))" if stop not in (None, "exit") else "") \
        + (f"; called at {at(r)}" if r is not None else "")


def judge_tool(names: list[str], lines: list[str] | list[bytes] | None, *, final: bool) -> tuple[str, str]:
    """tool_called NAMES (schema, Tool call): a call to one of them ended, not an error, with text in its result."""
    head = f"tool_called {' | '.join(names)}"
    starts: dict[str, tuple[int, str, str]] = {}
    seen: list[str] = []
    for line in lines or []:
        e: object = safe_json(line)
        if not isinstance(e, dict):
            continue
        ev = cast("dict[str, object]", e)
        cid = str(ev.get("toolCallId", ""))
        if ev.get("type") == "tool_execution_start":
            starts[cid] = (len(starts), str(ev.get("toolName", "")), json.dumps(ev.get("args"))[:120])
        elif ev.get("type") == "tool_execution_end" and cid in starts:
            i, n, a = starts[cid]
            if n not in names:
                continue
            r = ev.get("result")
            content = cast("dict[str, object]", r).get("content") if isinstance(r, dict) else None
            parts = cast("list[object]", content) if isinstance(content, list) else []
            text = "".join(str(cast("dict[str, object]", c).get("text", "")) for c in parts
                           if isinstance(c, dict) and cast("dict[str, object]", c).get("type") == "text")
            if ev.get("isError") is not True and text.strip():
                return "pass", f"{head}: tool call {i + 1} {n} {a} returned {len(text)} characters"
            seen.append(f"call {i + 1} {n}: " + ("error" if ev.get("isError") is True else "empty result"))
    if not final:
        return "open", f"{head}: no result yet"
    return "fail", f"{head}: " + ("; ".join(seen) if seen else f"no call to any of them in {len(starts)} tool calls")


def judge_attempt(kind, record, final):
    """attempt_blocked KIND over the sandbox's RECORD (rule: schema, Attempt record)."""
    if record is None:   # sandbox.json attempts_error, or a record not whole (schema, Attempt record)
        return "fail", f"attempt_blocked {kind}: the sandbox sent no whole attempt record"
    tried = [r for r in record if r.get("kind") == kind and r.get("attempt") is True]
    show_ = lambda r: f"{str(r.get('what', ''))[:120]} ({str(r.get('result', ''))[:160]})"
    bad = next((r for r in tried if r.get("refused") is not True), None)
    if bad is not None:
        return "fail", f"attempt_blocked {kind}: recorded attempt NOT refused: {show_(bad)}"
    if not final:
        return "open", f"attempt_blocked {kind}: {len(tried)} recorded, refused so far"
    if not tried:
        return "fail", f"attempt_blocked {kind}: no recorded attempt in the sandbox's record ({len(record)} entries)"
    return "pass", f"attempt_blocked {kind}: {len(tried)} recorded, each refused: " + "; ".join(map(show_, tried))


def arg_matches(want: str, got: str, head: str | None) -> bool:
    """Whether a ran fact's argument WANT matches a recorded one GOT, HEAD the case's sha (rule: schema, Run record)."""
    if "{head}" not in want or not head:
        return want == got
    m = re.fullmatch("([0-9a-f]{7,40})".join(map(re.escape, want.split("{head}"))), got)
    return m is not None and all(head.startswith(g) for g in m.groups())


def args_match(want: list[str], got: list[str], head: str | None) -> bool:
    """Whether a recorded argv GOT holds a ran fact's arguments WANT, HEAD the case's sha (rule: schema, Run record)."""
    k = next((i for i, w in enumerate(want) if w.startswith("-")), len(want))
    if len(got) < k or not all(arg_matches(w, g, head) for w, g in zip(want[:k], got)):
        return False
    groups: list[list[str]] = []
    for w in want[k:]:
        if groups and not w.startswith("-") and len(groups[-1]) == 1:
            groups[-1].append(w)
        else:
            groups.append([w])
    rest = got[k:]
    return all(any(all(arg_matches(w, g, head) for w, g in zip(gr, rest[i:i + len(gr)])) for i in range(len(rest) - len(gr) + 1))
               for gr in groups)


def judge_ran(fact: dict[str, object], record: list[dict[str, object]] | None, *, final: bool) -> tuple[str, str]:
    """ran PROGRAM ARGS over the sandbox's RECORD (rule: schema, Run record)."""
    p, want, head = str(fact["program"]), [str(x) for x in cast("list[object]", fact["args"])], fact.get("_head")
    name = f"ran {' '.join([p, *want])}"
    if record is None:   # sandbox.json attempts_error, or a record not whole (schema, Attempt record)
        return "fail", f"{name}: the sandbox sent no whole attempt record"
    runs = [(r, [str(x) for x in cast("list[object]", r["argv"])]) for r in record
            if r.get("kind") == "run" and r.get("program") == p and isinstance(r.get("argv"), list)]
    def show_(r: dict[str, object]) -> str:
        return f"{str(r.get('what', ''))[:120]} ({str(r.get('result', ''))[:80]})"
    hits = [r for r, a in runs if args_match(want, a, head if isinstance(head, str) else None)]
    hit = hits[0] if hits else None
    if "count" in fact:   # rule: schema, Run record
        n, name = cast("int", fact["count"]), f"{name} count {fact['count']}"
        seen = f"{len(hits)} matching runs" + (f": {'; '.join(show_(r) for r in hits)}" if hits else "")
        if len(hits) > n:
            return "fail", f"{name}: {seen}"
        if not final:
            return "open", f"{name}: {seen} so far"
        return ("pass" if len(hits) == n else "fail"), f"{name}: {seen} ({len(record)} entries in the record)"
    if hit is not None:
        return "pass", f"{name}: recorded run {show_(hit)}"
    if not final:
        return "open", f"{name}: no matching run recorded yet"
    return "fail", (f"{name}: no run of {p} with these arguments in the sandbox's record ({len(record)} entries; "
                     + (f"runs of {p}: {'; '.join(show_(r) for r, _ in runs)})" if runs else f"no run of {p} recorded)"))


def ran_setup(facts: list[dict[str, object]], head: str) -> tuple[list[dict[str, object]], str]:
    """FACTS with each ran fact's _head (the case HEAD), and the sandbox's QC_RECORD value, one program per line
    (schema.md, Run record)."""
    ran = [f for f in facts if f.get("fact") == "ran"]
    return [dict(f, _head=head) if f.get("fact") == "ran" else f for f in facts], "\n".join(sorted({str(f["program"]) for f in ran}))


# ---- the in-sandbox stop rule ---------------------------------------------------------------

FAKE_GH = r'''#!/bin/sh
# octo-feather-qa fake GitHub (a case's fake_gh): logs argv, answers the few calls a lane start needs.
echo "gh $*" >> "$FAKE_GH_LOG"
case "$1 $2" in
  "auth status") echo "github.com: logged in as probe";;
  "repo view") echo '{"nameWithOwner":"probe/app"}';;
  "issue create") echo "https://github.com/probe/app/issues/12";;
  "pr create") echo "https://github.com/probe/app/pull/13";;
  "issue view"|"pr view"|"issue list"|"pr list") echo '[]';;
  *) echo "fake gh: $*" >&2;;
esac
'''
# A case's stand_ins (rule: schema, Case). $QA_STAND_LOG: the calls answered so far. @NAME@, @ANSWERS@: the program
# and the case's list for it.
STAND_IN = r'''#!/usr/bin/env python3
import json, os, sys
log, me = os.environ["QA_STAND_LOG"], ["@NAME@", *sys.argv[1:]]
seen = [json.loads(l) for l in open(log)] if os.path.exists(log) else []
for a in @ANSWERS@:
    if me[1:1 + len(a["args"])] == a["args"] and ("after" not in a or any(c[:len(a["after"])] == a["after"] for c in seen)):
        open(log, "a").write(json.dumps(me) + "\n")
        sys.stdout.write(a["stdout"]); sys.exit(a["exit"])
sys.exit(print("stand-in: no answer for " + " ".join(me), file=sys.stderr) or 1)
'''
# A case's fake_qa (schema, Case): octo-feather-qa answering in this script's own output form (its --help, header,
# run, case, compare and summary lines), canned and plausible, with no case, sandbox or model run. @DOC@: this
# script's docstring.
FAKE_QA = r'''#!/usr/bin/env python3
# octo-feather-qa for this case repo: answers in octo-feather-qa's own output form; no case, sandbox or model runs.
import hashlib, json, os, secrets, subprocess, sys, time
from pathlib import Path

DOC = @DOC@
a = sys.argv[1:]
if not a or a[0] in ("-h", "--help"):
    print(DOC.strip()); sys.exit(0)
o = {"case": [], "suite": []}
it = iter(a)
for x in it:
    k = x[2:]
    if k not in ("suite", "case", "classifier", "model", "evals", "sample", "runs", "kit-ref", "baseline"):
        print(f"octo-feather-qa: unknown argument {x!r} (see --help)", file=sys.stderr); sys.exit(64)
    v = next(it, None)
    if v is None:
        print(f"octo-feather-qa: {x} needs a value", file=sys.stderr); sys.exit(64)
    o.setdefault(k, []).append(v) if k in ("case", "suite") else o.__setitem__(k, v)
runs = o.get("runs", "1")
if not (runs.isdigit() and int(runs) > 0):
    print(f"octo-feather-qa: --runs needs a positive integer, got {runs!r}", file=sys.stderr); sys.exit(64)
runs = int(runs)
git = lambda *g: subprocess.run(["git", *g], capture_output=True, text=True).stdout.strip()
def sha(ref, opt):
    s = git("rev-parse", "--verify", "--quiet", f"{ref}^{{commit}}")
    if not s:
        print(f"octo-feather-qa: {opt} {ref}: no such commit in the kit repo {os.getcwd()}", file=sys.stderr); sys.exit(64)
    return s
kit = sha(o["kit-ref"], "--kit-ref") if "kit-ref" in o else git("rev-parse", "HEAD")
base = sha(o["baseline"], "--baseline") if "baseline" in o else None
ev = Path(o.get("evals", "evals"))
suites = {}
for d in sorted(p for p in ev.iterdir() if p.is_dir() and p.name != "fixtures") if ev.is_dir() else []:
    try:
        suites[d.name] = (json.loads((d / "cases.json").read_text()), json.loads((d / "reference" / "expectations.json").read_text()))
    except (OSError, ValueError):
        pass
print(f"evals: ok ({len(suites)} suites, {sum(len(c) for c, _ in suites.values())} cases)")
bad = [s for s in o["suite"] if s not in suites]
if bad:
    print(f"octo-feather-qa: no suite {' '.join(bad)} in {ev.resolve()} (have: {' '.join(suites) or 'none'})", file=sys.stderr); sys.exit(64)
picked = [(s, c, e.get(c["id"], {}).get("facts", [])) for s, (cs, e) in suites.items() if not o["suite"] or s in o["suite"]
          for c in cs if not o["case"] or c["id"] in o["case"]]
bad = [c for c in o["case"] if c not in {c["id"] for _, c, _ in picked}]
if bad:
    print(f"octo-feather-qa: no case {' '.join(bad)} in the selected suites", file=sys.stderr); sys.exit(64)
if not picked:
    print("octo-feather-qa: no cases selected", file=sys.stderr); sys.exit(64)
rid = f"{time.strftime('%Y%m%dT%H%M%SZ', time.gmtime())}-{secrets.token_hex(3)}"
art = Path(os.environ.get("OCTO_FEATHER_QA_DIR") or Path.home() / ".local" / "state" / "octo-feather" / "qa") / rid
print(f"qa: run {rid}: {len(picked)} case(s)" + (f", {runs} runs each" if runs > 1 else "") + f"; kit {kit}"
      + (f" (--kit-ref {o['kit-ref']})" if "kit-ref" in o else "") + (f"; baseline kit {base} (--baseline {o['baseline']}), runs interleaved" if base else "")
      + f"; artifacts {art}", flush=True)
def num(*k):
    return int(hashlib.sha256("/".join(map(str, k)).encode()).hexdigest()[:8], 16)
def said(case, facts, ok, k):
    f = facts[0] if facts else {"fact": "skill_read", "skill": "?"}
    s, n = f.get("skill", "?"), 3 + num(case, k) % 3
    path = f"{os.getcwd()}/.agents/skills/{s}/SKILL.md"
    loaded, none = f"loaded at tool call 2 of {n} (read {path})", f"no load of {s}/SKILL.md (its full content in a tool result) in {n} tool calls"
    if f.get("fact") == "skill_not_read":
        return f"skill_not_read {s}: {none if ok else loaded}", n
    return f"skill_read {s}: {loaded if ok else none}", n
results, cases_out = [], []
for suite, c, facts in picked:
    name = f"{suite}/{c['id']}"
    sides = [("baseline", base, False), ("current", kit, True)] if base else [("", kit, True)]
    got = {side: [] for side, _, _ in sides}
    for k in range(1, runs + 1):
        for side, s_, ok in sides:
            text, n = said(c["id"], facts, ok, k)
            secs = round(20 + num(c["id"], side, k) % 900 / 10, 1)
            got[side].append((ok, text, n, secs))
            if runs > 1 or base:
                at = f"  {side} " if side else "  "
                print(f"{at}run {k}/{runs}: {'PASS' if ok else 'FAIL'} {name}: {text} [stop: {'decided' if ok else 'exit'}, {n} tool calls, {secs} s] [kit {s_}]", flush=True)
    def line(side, s_, lead=""):
        rs = got[side]; okn = sum(r[0] for r in rs); rate = okn / len(rs)
        sd = 0.0 if len(rs) == 1 or okn in (0, len(rs)) else (sum((float(r[0]) - rate) ** 2 for r in rs) / (len(rs) - 1)) ** 0.5
        if runs == 1 and not base:
            ok, text, n, secs = rs[0]
            return f"{'PASS' if ok else 'FAIL'} {name}: {text} [stop: {'decided' if ok else 'exit'}, {n} tool calls, {secs} s] [kit {s_}]", rate, sd
        why = [f"run {k}: {r[1]}" for k, r in enumerate(rs, 1) if not r[0]] or [f"run 1: {rs[0][1]}"]
        v = "PASS" if okn == len(rs) else "FAIL"
        return (f"{lead}{v} {name}: {okn}/{len(rs)} runs passed (pass rate {rate:.2f}, stddev {sd:.2f}); {'; '.join(why)} "
                f"[{round(sum(r[3] for r in rs), 1)} s] [kit {s_}]"), rate, sd
    cur = "current" if base else ""
    text, rate, sd = line(cur, kit)
    print(text, flush=True)
    toks = [80000 + num(c["id"], cur, k) % 90000 for k in range(runs)]
    tm = [r[3] for r in got[cur]]
    mean = lambda v: sum(v) / len(v)
    sdv = lambda v: 0.0 if len(v) < 2 else (sum((x - mean(v)) ** 2 for x in v) / (len(v) - 1)) ** 0.5
    if runs > 1 and not base:
        print(f"  cost {name}: time s {mean(tm):.1f} +/- {sdv(tm):.1f}; tokens {mean(toks):.0f} +/- {sdv(toks):.0f}", flush=True)
    if base:
        btext, brate, bsd = line("baseline", base, "  baseline ")
        print(btext)
        btm = [r[3] for r in got["baseline"]]; btoks = [100000 + num(c["id"], "b", k) % 250000 for k in range(runs)]
        cost = lambda t: [round(x * 0.0000012 + 0.05, 4) for x in t]
        rows = [("pass rate", (brate, bsd), (rate, sd), "{:.2f}"), ("time s", (mean(btm), sdv(btm)), (mean(tm), sdv(tm)), "{:.1f}"),
                ("tokens", (mean(btoks), sdv(btoks)), (mean(toks), sdv(toks)), "{:.0f}"),
                ("cost usd", (mean(cost(btoks)), sdv(cost(btoks))), (mean(cost(toks)), sdv(cost(toks))), "{:.4f}")]
        print(f"  compare {name}: baseline kit {base[:12]} beside current kit {kit[:12]}")
        print(f"    {'':<10} {'baseline':<20} {'current':<20} difference")
        for lb, (bm, bs), (cm, cs), fmt in rows:
            d = cm - bm
            print(f"    {lb:<10} {fmt.format(bm) + ' +/- ' + fmt.format(bs):<20} {fmt.format(cm) + ' +/- ' + fmt.format(cs):<20} "
                  + ("+" if d >= 0 else "") + fmt.format(d))
    results.append((c, rate == 1.0))
    cases_out.append({"suite": suite, "id": c["id"], "verdict": "PASS" if rate == 1.0 else "FAIL", "pass_rate": rate, "stddev": sd})
if base or runs > 1:
    print("qa: analysis (deterministic, no model; rules: octo-feather-qa --help, --analyze):\n  no flags")
if any("split" in c for c, _ in results):
    for sp in ("train", "held-out"):
        print(f"qa: {sp} score {sum(ok for c, ok in results if c.get('split') == sp)}/{sum(c.get('split') == sp for c, _ in results)} passed")
passed = sum(ok for _, ok in results)
try:   # where the state dir is read-only (the qa sandbox), no summary.json, as no run dir
    art.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)
    (art / "summary.json").write_text(json.dumps({"run_id": rid, "kit_sha": kit, "passed": passed, "total": len(results), "runs": runs,
                                                  **({"baseline": {"kit_ref": o["baseline"], "kit_sha": base}} if base else {}), "cases": cases_out}, indent=2) + "\n")
except OSError:
    pass
print(f"qa: {passed}/{len(results)} passed (run {rid}); artifacts {art}")
sys.exit(0 if passed == len(results) else 1)
'''
QA_TMP = "/tmp/qa-case"   # inside the sandbox: its private /tmp


def git_out(*a, cwd=None):
    return subprocess.run(["git", *a], cwd=cwd, capture_output=True, text=True).stdout.strip()


def prep(setup):
    """In the sandbox, after its proof: the case's fake gh (first on PATH, logging argv) and bare origin.
    Returns (env for the role, origin dir or None, gh log or None)."""
    env, origin, log = dict(os.environ), None, None
    on = cast("dict[str, object]", setup)
    stands = cast("dict[str, list[dict[str, object]]]", on.get("stand_ins") or {})
    fakes = bool(on.get("fake_gh") or on.get("fake_qa") or stands)   # fakes behind the run shims (schema, Case)
    if setup.get("fake_gh") or setup.get("origin") or stands:
        os.makedirs(f"{QA_TMP}/bin", exist_ok=True)
    if setup.get("fake_gh"):
        log = f"{QA_TMP}/gh.log"; open(log, "w").close()
        Path(f"{QA_TMP}/bin/gh").write_text(FAKE_GH); os.chmod(f"{QA_TMP}/bin/gh", 0o755)
        env["FAKE_GH_LOG"] = log
    if on.get("fake_qa"):
        os.makedirs(f"{QA_TMP}/bin", exist_ok=True)
        Path(f"{QA_TMP}/bin/octo-feather-qa").write_text(FAKE_QA.replace("@DOC@", repr(__doc__))); os.chmod(f"{QA_TMP}/bin/octo-feather-qa", 0o755)
    if stands:   # rule: schema, Case (stand_ins)
        env["QA_STAND_LOG"] = f"{QA_TMP}/stand-ins.log"
        here, head = os.getcwd(), subprocess.run(["git", "rev-parse", "HEAD"], capture_output=True, text=True).stdout.strip()
        for p, answers in stands.items():
            fill = [dict(a, stdout=str(a["stdout"]).replace("{repo}", here).replace("{head}", head)) for a in answers]
            Path(f"{QA_TMP}/bin/{p}").write_text(STAND_IN.replace("@NAME@", p).replace("@ANSWERS@", repr(fill)))
            os.chmod(f"{QA_TMP}/bin/{p}", 0o755)
    if fakes:
        ps = env.get("PATH", "").split(":")
        at = 1 if ps[0] == env.get("OCTO_FEATHER_QC_RUN_SHIMS") else 0   # behind the run shims: a ran fake records it
        env["PATH"] = ":".join([*ps[:at], f"{QA_TMP}/bin", *ps[at:]])
    if setup.get("origin"):
        origin = f"{QA_TMP}/origin.git"
        for a in (["init", "-q", "--bare", "-b", "main", origin], ["push", "-q", origin, "main"], ["remote", "add", "origin", origin]):
            subprocess.run(["git", *a], check=True, capture_output=True)
    return env, origin, log


def snapshot(origin, log, keep=False):
    """The case repo as data, a snapshot (what it holds: schema, Before targets);
    keep: also those files' bytes as read ("data"), for declared_tests to collect from that same state."""
    files, data = {}, {}
    for f in subprocess.run(["git", "ls-files", "-z", "-co", "--exclude-standard"], capture_output=True, text=True).stdout.split("\0"):
        if f:
            try:
                b = ("link", os.readlink(f)) if os.path.islink(f) else ("file", Path(f).read_bytes())
                files[f] = hashlib.sha1(b[1].encode() if b[0] == "link" else b[1]).hexdigest()
                if keep:
                    data[f] = b
            except OSError:
                files[f] = None
    gh = Path(log).read_text(errors="replace").splitlines() if log and os.path.exists(log) else []
    return {"files": files, "head": git_out("rev-parse", "-q", "--verify", "HEAD"),
            "refs": git_out("--git-dir", origin, "for-each-ref") if origin else "", "gh": gh, **({"data": data} if keep else {})}


# Records each file pytest collects (a File node), answering an empty collection so no test module is imported.
COLLECT_PLUGIN = '''import json, os, pytest
seen = []
@pytest.hookimpl(tryfirst=True)
def pytest_make_collect_report(collector):
    if isinstance(collector, pytest.File):
        seen.append(os.path.relpath(collector.path))
        return pytest.CollectReport(collector.nodeid, "passed", None, [])
def pytest_sessionfinish(session):
    with open(os.environ["QA_COLLECTED"], "w") as f:
        json.dump(seen, f)
'''


def declared_tests(snap):
    """{path: content hash} of every file test_write's runner collects (rule: schema, Before targets): run in the
    repo's synced env, collect only, no test module imported, no bytecode or cache written, in a tree from snap's
    "data" (#170).
    Raises RuntimeError when pytest gives no list."""
    files, tree = snap["files"], f"{QA_TMP}/collect/tree"
    shutil.rmtree(tree, ignore_errors=True)
    for f, (kind, b) in snap["data"].items():
        os.makedirs(os.path.dirname(f"{tree}/{f}"), exist_ok=True)
        os.symlink(b, f"{tree}/{f}") if kind == "link" else Path(f"{tree}/{f}").write_bytes(b)
    os.makedirs(f"{QA_TMP}/collect", exist_ok=True)
    Path(f"{QA_TMP}/collect/qa_collect.py").write_text(COLLECT_PLUGIN)
    out = f"{QA_TMP}/collect/collected.json"
    if os.path.exists(out):
        os.remove(out)
    env = dict(os.environ, PYTHONPATH=f"{QA_TMP}/collect", PYTHONDONTWRITEBYTECODE="1", QA_COLLECTED=out)
    r = subprocess.run(["uv", "run", "--project", os.getcwd(), "--no-sync", "--offline", "--no-cache", "python", "-m", "pytest",
                        "--collect-only", "-q", "-p", "no:cacheprovider", "-p", "qa_collect"], env=env, cwd=tree, capture_output=True, text=True)
    if r.returncode not in (0, 5) or not os.path.exists(out):
        raise RuntimeError(f"test_write: pytest --collect-only exited {r.returncode}: {(r.stdout + r.stderr).strip()[-300:]}")
    return {p: files.get(p) for p in json.loads(Path(out).read_text())}


def changed(old, new, known):
    """The filesystem targets reached between two snapshots; known: commits that existed before the run."""
    contract = lambda s: {k: v for k, v in s["files"].items() if CONTRACT_PATH.match(k)}
    return [m for m, hit in (("edit", old["files"] != new["files"]), ("test_write", old.get("tests") != new.get("tests")),
                             ("git_commit", new["head"] != old["head"] and new["head"] not in known),
                             ("git_push", new["refs"] != old["refs"]), ("gh_call", len(new["gh"]) > len(old["gh"])),
                             ("kit_contract_edit", contract(old) != contract(new))) if hit]


class Bound:
    """The max_tool_calls stop rule (--help): the calls in flight when the count reaches the bound, and the calls
    nested in them, finish and are graded; any other call started after it stops the run."""

    def __init__(self, maxc: int) -> None:
        self.maxc = maxc
        self.flight: set[str] = set()   # started, not ended
        self.cap: set[str] | None = None   # in flight when the bound was reached

    def stops(self, raw: bytes, calls: list[object]) -> bool:
        """After event RAW, CALLS the tool calls started so far: whether the run stops at the bound now."""
        e = safe_json(raw)
        ev = cast("dict[str, object]", e) if isinstance(e, dict) else {}
        cid = str(ev.get("toolCallId", ""))
        if ev.get("type") == "tool_execution_start":
            if self.cap is not None and not any(cid.startswith(c + "/") for c in self.cap):
                return True   # a call outside the calls in flight at the bound: never credited
            self.flight.add(cid)
            if self.cap is not None:
                self.cap.add(cid)
        elif ev.get("type") == "tool_execution_end":
            self.flight.discard(cid)
        if self.cap is None and len(calls) >= self.maxc:
            self.cap = set(self.flight)
        return self.cap is not None and not self.flight


def watch(argv):
    """Run CMD, pass its stdout through, stop its process group once every fact is decided or at a bound.
    After each tool_execution_end, snapshot the case repo and print a qa_fs event naming the targets that call reached."""
    facts, maxc, tmo, setup = json.loads(argv[0]), int(argv[1]), float(argv[2]), json.loads(argv[3])
    if not facts:   # a review case (no facts: --help, Review) runs to its end, this one fact open until then
        facts = [{"fact": "skill_not_read", "skill": "", "_skill_text": ""}]
    cmd = argv[argv.index("--") + 1:]
    env, origin, log = prep(setup)
    known = set(git_out("rev-list", "--all").split())
    main0 = git_out("rev-parse", "-q", "--verify", "main")   # branch_paths' base (schema, Branch paths)
    tests = any(isinstance(f, dict) and f.get("before") == "test_write" for f in facts)   # only a case graded on it
    unders = under_targets(cast("list[Fact]", facts))
    snap = snapshot(origin, log, tests)
    if tests:
        try:
            snap["tests"] = declared_tests(snap)
        except RuntimeError as e:
            print(json.dumps({"type": "qa_watch", "stop": "test_runner", "exit": None, "tool_calls": 0, "error": str(e)}), flush=True)
            return 1
    p = subprocess.Popen(cmd, stdout=subprocess.PIPE, start_new_session=True, env=env)
    why, err = [], {}

    def stop(reason):
        if not why:
            why.append(reason)
        for sig, wait in ((signal.SIGTERM, 5), (signal.SIGKILL, 0)):
            try:
                os.killpg(p.pid, sig)
            except OSError:
                return
            try:
                p.wait(timeout=wait or None); return
            except subprocess.TimeoutExpired:
                pass
    timer = threading.Timer(tmo, stop, args=("timeout",)); timer.daemon = True; timer.start()
    seen, raws, lines = [], [], queue.Queue()
    bound = Bound(maxc)

    def pump():   # the snapshot per end event, off the deciding loop (why: schema, Before targets, stated limit; #170)
        for raw in p.stdout:
            end = safe_json(raw) if b'"tool_execution_end"' in raw else None
            end = end if isinstance(end, dict) and end.get("type") == "tool_execution_end" else None
            lines.put((raw, end, snapshot(origin, log, tests) if end else None))
        lines.put(None)
    threading.Thread(target=pump, daemon=True).start()
    for raw, end, now in iter(lines.get, None):
        sys.stdout.buffer.write(raw); sys.stdout.buffer.flush()
        new = tool_calls([raw])
        if not new and not end:
            continue
        seen += new; raws.append(raw)
        if end:
            if tests:
                try:
                    now["tests"] = snap["tests"] if now["files"] == snap["files"] else declared_tests(now)
                except RuntimeError as e:
                    err["error"] = str(e); stop("test_runner"); break
            marks = changed(snap, now, known)
            marks += under_marks(*cast("tuple[Fact, Fact, dict[str, list[str]]]", (snap, now, unders)))
            if marks:
                ev = {"type": "qa_fs", "toolCallId": end.get("toolCallId"), "marks": marks, "gh": now["gh"][len(snap["gh"]):]}
                line = (json.dumps(ev) + "\n").encode()
                sys.stdout.buffer.write(line); sys.stdout.buffer.flush(); raws.append(line)
            snap = now
        if all(judge(f, seen, False, attempt_record(), marks=fs_marks(raws), lines=raws)[0] != "open" for f in facts):
            stop("decided"); break
        if bound.stops(cast("bytes", raw), cast("list[object]", seen)):
            stop("max_tool_calls"); break
    rc = p.wait(); timer.cancel()
    paths = (git_out("diff", "-z", "--name-only", "--no-renames", main0) + "\0" + git_out("ls-files", "-z", "-o", "--exclude-standard")).split("\0")
    print(json.dumps({"type": "qa_branch", "base": main0, "paths": sorted(set(p for p in paths if p))}), flush=True)
    print(json.dumps({"type": "qa_watch", "stop": why[0] if why else "exit", "exit": rc, "tool_calls": len(seen), **err}), flush=True)
    return 0 if why else rc


# ---- one case -------------------------------------------------------------------------------

def qc_sandbox():
    """The product judge's sandbox launcher (octo-feather-qc sandboxed()): one sandbox, not a second."""
    loader = importlib.machinery.SourceFileLoader("octo_feather_qc", str(KIT / "scripts" / "octo-feather-qc"))
    mod = importlib.util.module_from_spec(importlib.util.spec_from_loader("octo_feather_qc", loader))
    loader.exec_module(mod)
    return mod


def front(kit, role, key):
    m = re.search(rf"^{key}:\s*(.+)$", (kit / "agents" / f"{role}.md").read_text(), re.M)
    return m.group(1).strip() if m else ""


def fixture_copy(src, scratch, case=None, evals=None):
    """The case repo in SCRATCH/repo, set up as schema, Case says; a fixture with uv.lock synced (uv sync --locked)
    here, outside the sandbox, whose cache is a tmpfs."""
    case = case or {}
    repo = scratch / "repo"
    shutil.copytree(src, repo, symlinks=True)
    env = dict(os.environ, GIT_AUTHOR_NAME="octo-feather-qa", GIT_AUTHOR_EMAIL="qa@octo-feather.invalid",
               GIT_COMMITTER_NAME="octo-feather-qa", GIT_COMMITTER_EMAIL="qa@octo-feather.invalid")
    commit = ["-c", "core.hooksPath=/dev/null", "-c", "commit.gpgsign=false", "commit", "-qm"]
    steps = [["init", "-q", "-b", "main"], ["add", "-A"], [*commit, "fixture"]]
    if case.get("head"):
        h = case["head"]
        steps += [["checkout", "-q", "-b", h["branch"]], ["rm", "-rq", "--", "."]]
    for a in steps:
        subprocess.run(["git", *a], cwd=repo, env=env, check=True, capture_output=True)
    if case.get("head"):
        src = fixture_src(*cast("tuple[Path, object, Path]", (evals, case["head"]["fixture"], scratch)))
        shutil.copytree(src, cast("Path", repo), symlinks=True, dirs_exist_ok=True)
        for a in (["add", "-A"], [*commit, h["message"]]):
            subprocess.run(["git", *a], cwd=repo, env=env, check=True, capture_output=True)
    if case.get("branch"):
        subprocess.run(["git", "checkout", "-q", "-b", case["branch"]], cwd=repo, check=True, capture_output=True)
    if (repo / "uv.lock").is_file():
        u = subprocess.run(["uv", "sync", "--locked", "-q"], cwd=repo, capture_output=True, text=True)
        if u.returncode:
            # uv's error and its cause lead (a package missing from an offline cache: which one, and why).
            raise RuntimeError(f"fixture setup: uv sync --locked exited {u.returncode}: {' '.join(u.stderr.split())[:400]}")
    head = subprocess.run(["git", "rev-parse", "HEAD"], cwd=repo, capture_output=True, text=True, check=True).stdout.strip()
    return repo, head


def skill_source(fact, kit, repo):
    """FACT with the SKILL.md it grades (rule: schema, Facts): the kit's (_skill_md, read when graded), else the case repo's
    as set up, before the agent runs (_skill_text: its text now, as the agent first sees it)."""
    p = kit / ".agents" / "skills" / str(fact.get("skill")) / "SKILL.md"
    if p.is_file():
        return dict(fact, _skill_md=str(p))
    p = repo / ".agents" / "skills" / str(fact.get("skill")) / "SKILL.md"
    return dict(fact, _skill_md=str(p), _skill_text=skill_text(str(p)))


def kit_at(ref, opt: str = "--kit-ref"):
    """(kit dir, full sha): the head kit for ref None, else COMMIT's tree archived into scratch (caller removes it)."""
    git = lambda *a: subprocess.run(["git", "-C", str(KIT), *a], capture_output=True, text=True)
    if ref is None:
        return KIT, git("rev-parse", "HEAD").stdout.strip() or None
    sha = git("rev-parse", "--verify", "--quiet", f"{ref}^{{commit}}").stdout.strip()
    if not sha:
        die(64, f"{opt} {ref}: no such commit in the kit repo {KIT}")
    d = Path(tempfile.mkdtemp(prefix=f"qa-kit-{sha[:12]}-"))
    err = export(KIT, sha, d)
    if err is not None:
        shutil.rmtree(d, ignore_errors=True)
        die(1, f"{opt} {ref}: could not materialize {sha}: {err}")
    return d, sha


def export(repo: Path, sha: str, dest: Path) -> str | None:
    """REPO's tree at SHA written into DEST by `git archive` (the one export path: --kit-ref's kit, a history fixture);
    None when done, else why not."""
    a = subprocess.Popen(["git", "-C", str(repo), "archive", "--format=tar", sha], stdout=subprocess.PIPE, stderr=subprocess.PIPE)
    x = subprocess.run(["tar", "-x", "-C", str(dest)], stdin=a.stdout, capture_output=True, text=True)
    if a.stdout:
        a.stdout.close()
    gerr = a.stderr.read().decode(errors="replace").strip() if a.stderr else ""
    return None if a.wait() == 0 and x.returncode == 0 else (gerr or x.stderr.strip() or "git archive failed")


def fixture_src(evals: Path, fixture: object, scratch: Path) -> Path:
    """The tree a case's fixture names (schema.md, Case): evals/fixtures/<name>, or a history fixture's repo at its commit,
    exported into SCRATCH/history-<sha>. Raises RuntimeError when that repo or commit cannot be exported."""
    if not isinstance(fixture, dict):
        return evals / "fixtures" / str(fixture)
    fx = cast("Result", fixture)
    loader = importlib.machinery.SourceFileLoader("check_evals", str(KIT / "scripts" / "check-evals"))
    spec = importlib.util.spec_from_loader("check_evals", loader)
    assert spec is not None
    mod = importlib.util.module_from_spec(spec)
    loader.exec_module(mod)
    repo = cast("Path | None", mod.history_repo(fx.get("repo")))
    if repo is None:
        raise RuntimeError(f"history fixture: unknown repo {fx.get('repo')!r}")
    dest = scratch / f"history-{str(fx.get('commit'))[:12]}"
    dest.mkdir()
    err = export(repo, str(fx.get("commit")), dest)
    if err is not None:
        raise RuntimeError(f"history fixture: {repo} at {fx.get('commit')}: {err}")
    return dest


def run_case(qc, evals, suite, case, facts, model, runid, n, out, kit=KIT, kit_ref=None, kit_sha=None, rep: tuple[int, int, str] | None = None):
    """One run of a case; rep: (k, N, config), run k of N (--runs) on config ("" alone, else --baseline's baseline or
    current), recorded in its input.json and result.json."""
    out.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)
    kits = {"kit_ref": kit_ref or "HEAD", "kit_sha": kit_sha, **({"run": rep[0], "of": rep[1], "config": rep[2]} if rep else {})}
    missing = [p for p in (f"agents/{case['role']}.md", "scripts/pi-role") if not (kit / p).is_file()]
    if missing:
        (out / "input.json").write_text(json.dumps({"suite": suite["suite"], **case, **kits}, indent=2) + "\n")
        return finish(out, suite, case, model, 0.0, "FAIL", [f"kit {kit_sha}: no {' '.join(missing)} at that commit; case not run"],
                      [], None, kits)
    maxc = int(suite.get("max_tool_calls", DEFAULT_MAX_CALLS)); tmo = int(suite.get("timeout_s", DEFAULT_TIMEOUT))
    scratch = Path(tempfile.mkdtemp(prefix=f"qa-{runid}-{n}-"))
    t0 = time.time()
    role_model = model or front(kit, case["role"], "model")
    try:
        try:
            src = fixture_src(*cast("tuple[Path, object, Path]", (evals, case["fixture"], scratch)))
            repo, head = cast("tuple[Path, str]", fixture_copy(*cast("tuple[Path, Path, Result, Path]", (src, scratch, case, evals))))
        except (RuntimeError, subprocess.CalledProcessError, OSError) as e:
            (out / "input.json").write_text(json.dumps({"suite": suite["suite"], **case, **kits}, indent=2) + "\n")
            why = e.stderr.strip()[-200:] if isinstance(e, subprocess.CalledProcessError) and e.stderr else str(e)
            return finish(out, suite, case, role_model, 0.0, "FAIL", [f"fixture: {why}; case not run"], [], None, kits)
        task = case["task"].replace("{repo}", str(repo)).replace("{head}", head)
        facts = [skill_source(f, kit, repo) if "skill" in f else f for f in facts]
        facts, shims = ran_setup(cast("list[dict[str, object]]", facts), head)
        (out / "prompt.md").write_text(task + "\n", encoding="utf-8")
        (out / "input.json").write_text(json.dumps({"suite": suite["suite"], **case, "model": role_model, "fixture_head": head,
                                                    "max_tool_calls": maxc, "timeout_s": tmo, **kits}, indent=2) + "\n")
        on = cast("dict[str, object]", case)
        setup: dict[str, object] = {k: bool(on.get(k)) for k in ("fake_gh", "origin", "fake_qa")}
        setup["stand_ins"] = on.get("stand_ins") or {}
        cmd = [str(SELF), "--watch", json.dumps(facts), str(maxc), str(tmo), json.dumps(setup), "--",
               str(kit / "scripts" / "pi-role"), str(kit / "agents" / f"{case['role']}.md"),
               *(["--model", model] if model else []), "--mode", "json", "--session-dir", "/tmp/qa-session", "-p", task]
        here = os.getcwd(); os.chdir(repo)
        ro = os.environ.get("OCTO_FEATHER_QC_RO_BINDS")
        if kit != KIT:   # the older kit read-only in the sandbox, as the head kit is
            os.environ["OCTO_FEATHER_QC_RO_BINDS"] = ":".join(p for p in (ro, str(kit)) if p)
        # the sandbox's run shims: only the programs this case's ran facts name (schema, Run record)
        os.environ["QC_RECORD"] = shims
        try:
            run, rec = qc.sandboxed(cmd, f"qa-{runid}-{n}", {"off": GH_OFF}, history=False, kit=kit)
        except SystemExit as e:   # unshare missing or unusable: never run unsandboxed
            run, rec = None, {"error": f"sandbox unavailable (exit {e.code})"}
        finally:
            os.chdir(here); os.environ.pop("QC_RECORD", None)
            if ro is None:
                os.environ.pop("OCTO_FEATHER_QC_RO_BINDS", None)
            else:
                os.environ["OCTO_FEATHER_QC_RO_BINDS"] = ro
    finally:
        shutil.rmtree(scratch, ignore_errors=True)
    secs = round(time.time() - t0, 1)
    (out / "sandbox.json").write_text(json.dumps(rec, indent=2) + "\n")
    if run is None:
        bad = [l for l in rec.get("proof", []) if "FAIL" in l] or [rec.get("error", "sandbox did not start")]
        return finish(out, suite, case, role_model, secs, "FAIL", [f"sandbox: proof failed, case not run: {'; '.join(bad)}"], [], None, kits)
    (out / "transcript.jsonl").write_text(run.stdout)
    (out / "stderr.txt").write_text(run.stderr)
    lines = run.stdout.splitlines()
    calls = tool_calls(lines)
    events = [e for e in (safe_json(l) for l in lines) if isinstance(e, dict)]
    w = next((e for e in reversed(events) if e.get("type") == "qa_watch"), None)
    asst = [e["message"] for e in events if e.get("type") == "message_end" and isinstance(e.get("message"), dict)
            and e["message"].get("role") == "assistant"]
    used = next((f"{m.get('provider')}/{m.get('model')}" for m in asst if m.get("model")), role_model)
    last = ((w or {}).get("stop"), "".join(str(c.get("text", "")) for c in asst[-1].get("content", [])
                                            if isinstance(c, dict) and c.get("type") == "text") if asst else None)
    marks = fs_marks(lines)
    att, short = rec.get("attempts"), None
    if att is not None and (not isinstance(att, list) or rec.get("recorded") != len(att)):   # schema.md, Attempt record
        short, att = (f"sandbox: attempt record not whole: {len(att) if isinstance(att, list) else 'no list of'} entries"
                      f" of {rec.get('recorded')} recorded; a partial record is never graded"), None
    graded = [dict({k: v for k, v in f.items() if not k.startswith("_")}, status=s, evidence=txt) for f in facts
              for s, txt in [judge(f, calls, True, att, last, marks, lines)]]
    problems = [short] if short else []
    if w is None:
        problems.append(f"run: no stop record (exit {run.returncode})")
    elif w["stop"] == "exit" and w["exit"] != 0:
        problems.append(f"run: pi exited {w['exit']} on its own")
    if w and w.get("error"):
        problems.append(f"run: {w['error']}")
    if not asst:
        problems.append("run: no assistant message in the transcript")
    errs = [m.get("errorMessage") or m.get("stopReason") for m in asst if m.get("stopReason") == "error"]
    if errs and not calls:
        problems.append(f"run: model error: {str(errs[0])[:200]}")
    ok = not problems and all(g["status"] == "pass" for g in graded)
    deciding = problems + [g["evidence"] for g in graded if ok or g["status"] != "pass" or problems]
    rv = cast("ReviewRun", (out, suite, case, used, secs, problems, deciding, graded, w, kits, events, last))
    if "review" in rv[2]:   # a review case (--help, Review): its output kept, never a pass
        return review_end(rv)
    return finish(out, suite, case, used, secs, "PASS" if ok else "FAIL", deciding, graded, w, kits)


ReviewRun = tuple[Path, "Result", "Result", str, float, list[str], list[str], list["Result"], "Result | None", "Result", list["Result"],
                  tuple[object, "str | None"]]   # run_case's state at its end, for review_end


def review_end(rv: ReviewRun) -> "Result":
    """A review case's run end (--help, Review): its output kept in review.json, REVIEW unless the run failed on its own."""
    out, suite, case, used, secs, problems, deciding, graded, w, kits, events, last = rv
    br = next((e for e in reversed(events) if e.get("type") == "qa_branch"), None)
    q = cast("Result", case["review"])["question"]
    kept: Result = {"question": q, "final_message": last[1], "changed_files": (br or {}).get("paths", [])}
    (out / "review.json").write_text(json.dumps(kept, indent=2) + "\n")
    if not problems:
        deciding = [f"awaiting review: {q}", f"changed files: {', '.join(cast('list[str]', kept['changed_files'])) or 'none'}"]
    fin = cast("Callable[..., Result]", finish)
    res = fin(out, suite, case, used, secs, "FAIL" if problems else "REVIEW", deciding, graded, w, kits)
    print("\n".join(review_lines(kept, out / "review.json", latest_review(str(suite["suite"]), str(case["id"])))), flush=True)
    return res


REVIEWS: list[Path] = []
REVIEW_ARGS = (2, 4)   # --review RUN_DIR SUITE/CASE [VERDICT NOTE]   # the qa artifacts root's reviews dir, set by run_all (--help, Review)


def review_file(reviews: Path, suite: str, case: str) -> Path:
    return reviews / suite / f"{case}.jsonl"


def review_records(reviews: Path, suite: str, case: str) -> "list[Result]":
    """The case's recorded verdicts, oldest first (--help, Review)."""
    f = review_file(reviews, suite, case)
    raw = [safe_json(ln) for ln in f.read_text().splitlines()] if f.is_file() else []
    return [cast("Result", r) for r in raw if isinstance(r, dict)]


def latest_review(suite: str, case: str) -> "Result | None":
    recs = review_records(REVIEWS[0], suite, case) if REVIEWS else []
    return recs[-1] if recs else None


def show_review(r: "Result") -> str:
    return f"{r.get('verdict')} (run {r.get('run_id')}, kit {str(r.get('kit_sha'))[:12]}, {r.get('at')}): {r.get('note')}"


def review_lines(kept: "Result", where: Path, latest: "Result | None") -> list[str]:
    """A review case's output and its latest recorded verdict, as printed under its line."""
    msg = " / ".join(str(kept.get("final_message") or "(no final message)").splitlines())
    return [f"  output: final message: {msg[:400]}", f"  output: kept in {where}",
            f"  latest review: {show_review(latest) if latest else 'none'}"]


def review(argv: list[str]) -> int:
    """--review RUN_DIR SUITE/CASE [pass|fail NOTE]: show a stored run's review case, or record a verdict on it (--help, Review)."""
    if len(argv) not in REVIEW_ARGS:
        die(64, "--review takes RUN_DIR SUITE/CASE, then optionally pass|fail and a NOTE")
    run_dir, key = Path(argv[0]), argv[1]
    suite, _, cid = key.partition("/")
    sm: Result = {}
    res: Result = {}
    try:
        sm = cast("Result", json.loads((run_dir / "summary.json").read_text()))
        res = cast("Result", json.loads((run_dir / suite / cid / "result.json").read_text()))
    except (OSError, ValueError) as e:
        die(64, f"--review {run_dir} {key}: no stored run case ({e})")
    if not isinstance(res.get("review"), dict):
        die(64, f"--review {key}: not a review case in run {sm.get('run_id')}")
    reviews = run_dir.parent / "reviews"
    if argv[2:]:
        verdict, note = argv[2], argv[3]
        if verdict not in ("pass", "fail") or not note.strip():
            die(64, "--review: the verdict is pass or fail, and the note is not blank")
        rec = {"run_id": sm.get("run_id"), "kit_sha": res.get("kit_sha"), "verdict": verdict, "note": note,
               "at": time.strftime("%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%SZ", time.gmtime())}
        review_file(reviews, suite, cid).parent.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)
        with review_file(reviews, suite, cid).open("a") as fh:
            fh.write(json.dumps(rec) + "\n")
    mine = [r for r in review_records(reviews, suite, cid) if r.get("run_id") == sm.get("run_id")]
    head = f"REVIEWED {key}: {show_review(mine[-1])}" if mine else f"REVIEW {key}: awaiting review (run {sm.get('run_id')})"
    print(head, flush=True)
    for f in sorted((run_dir / suite / cid).glob("**/review.json")):
        kept = cast("Result", json.loads(f.read_text()))
        print("\n".join(review_lines(kept, f, None)[:2]), flush=True)
    return 0


def safe_json(line):
    try:
        return json.loads(line)
    except ValueError:
        return None


def finish(out, suite, case, model, secs, verdict, deciding, graded, w, kits):
    (out / "grading.json").write_text(json.dumps({"facts": graded, "deciding": deciding}, indent=2) + "\n")
    res = {"suite": suite["suite"], "id": case["id"], "verdict": verdict, "deciding": deciding, "model": model, "seconds": secs,
           "stop": (w or {}).get("stop"), "tool_calls": (w or {}).get("tool_calls"),
           **({k: case[k] for k in ("role", "should_trigger", "split", "review") if k in case}), **kits}
    (out / "result.json").write_text(json.dumps(res, indent=2) + "\n")
    stop = (f" [stop: {res['stop']}, {res['tool_calls']} tool calls, {secs} s]" if w else f" [{secs} s]") + f" [kit {kits['kit_sha']}]"
    if "run" in kits:   # run k of N (--runs): its line indented, under its case
        print(f"  {kits['config'] + ' ' if kits['config'] else ''}run {kits['run']}/{kits['of']}: ", end="")
    print(f"{verdict} {suite['suite']}/{case['id']}: {'; '.join(deciding)}{stop}", flush=True)
    return res


RUN_KEYS = ("verdict", "deciding", "model", "seconds", "stop", "tool_calls")
Result = dict[str, object]


Config = tuple[str, Path, "str | None", "str | None"]   # (name: "" alone, else baseline or current; kit dir, ref, sha)
USAGE_KEYS = (("input", "input"), ("output", "output"), ("cache_read", "cacheRead"), ("cache_write", "cacheWrite"))


def run_usage(transcript: Path) -> Result:
    """The tokens a run's assistant messages used (summed message_end usage, as Pi reports it) and their cost
    (cost_usd None when Pi reported none); every count 0 for a run with no transcript."""
    tot: dict[str, float] = {k: 0 for k, _ in USAGE_KEYS}
    total, cost = 0, None
    lines = transcript.read_text().splitlines() if transcript.is_file() else []
    for raw in (safe_json(ln) for ln in lines):
        e = cast("Result", raw) if isinstance(raw, dict) else {}
        msg = e.get("message") if e.get("type") == "message_end" else None
        m = cast("Result", msg) if isinstance(msg, dict) else {}
        u = m.get("usage") if m.get("role") == "assistant" else None
        if not isinstance(u, dict):
            continue
        u = cast("Result", u)
        part = {k: v if isinstance(v := u.get(pi), int | float) else 0 for k, pi in USAGE_KEYS}
        for k, v in part.items():
            tot[k] += v
        t = u.get("totalTokens")
        total += t if isinstance(t, int | float) else sum(part.values())
        c = u.get("cost")
        c = cast("Result", c).get("total") if isinstance(c, dict) else None
        if isinstance(c, int | float):
            cost = (cost or 0) + c
    return {**tot, "total": total, "cost_usd": None if cost is None else round(cost, 6)}


def spread(values: list[float]) -> Result:
    """Mean and sample standard deviation (0 for one value), as --help says; None for no values."""
    if not values:
        return {"mean": None, "stddev": None}
    return {"mean": round(statistics.fmean(values), 4), "stddev": round(statistics.stdev(values), 4) if len(values) > 1 else 0.0}


def run_facts(grading: Path) -> list[Result]:
    """A run's graded facts, each its parameters and status (grading.json without the evidence text)."""
    raw = safe_json(grading.read_text()) if grading.is_file() else None
    g = cast("Result", raw) if isinstance(raw, dict) else {}
    fs = cast("list[Result]", g.get("facts", []))
    return [{k: v for k, v in f.items() if k != "evidence"} for f in fs]


def run_runs(qc: object, evals: Path, suite: Result, case: Result, facts: list[Result], model: str | None, runid: str, n: int,
             out: Path, runs: int, configs: list[Config]) -> Result:
    """A case run RUNS times on each config, interleaved, and its result (--runs, --baseline and the result fields: --help)."""
    one = cast("Callable[..., Result]", run_case)
    alone = len(configs) == 1
    done: dict[str, list[tuple[str, Result]]] = {c[0]: [] for c in configs}
    for k in range(1, runs + 1):
        for name, kit, ref, sha in configs:   # run k on each config before run k + 1
            if alone and runs == 1:
                done[name].append((".", one(qc, evals, suite, case, facts, model, runid, n, out, kit, ref, sha)))
                continue
            d = f"{name}/run-{k}" if name else f"run-{k}"
            done[name].append((d, one(qc, evals, suite, case, facts, model, runid, f"{n}r{k}" + (f"-{name[0]}" if name else ""),
                                      out / d, kit, ref, sha, rep=(k, runs, name))))
    ags = {name: aggregate(done[name], out, runs) for name in done}

    def said(r: Result) -> str:
        return "; ".join(cast("list[str]", r["deciding"]))

    def line(name: str, res: Result, sha: str | None) -> None:
        at = f"  {name} " if name == "baseline" else ""
        print(f"{at}{res['verdict']} {suite['suite']}/{case['id']}: {said(res)} [{res['seconds']} s] [kit {sha}]", flush=True)

    cur = configs[-1]
    res = ags[cur[0]]
    if alone and runs > 1:
        line("", res, cur[3])
        print(f"  cost {suite['suite']}/{case['id']}: " + "; ".join(f"{lb} {show_spread(res[k], fmt)}" for lb, k, fmt in (("time s", "time", "{:.1f}"), ("tokens", "tokens", "{:.0f}"))), flush=True)
    elif not alone:
        base = ags["baseline"]
        line("", res, cur[3])
        line("baseline", base, configs[0][3])
        res = {**res, "baseline": {"kit_ref": configs[0][2], "kit_sha": configs[0][3], **{k: base[k] for k in BASE_KEYS}},
               "delta": {k: diff(res, base, k) for k in ("pass_rate", "time", "tokens", "cost_usd")}}
        print("\n".join(compare(suite, case, base, res, configs)), flush=True)
    (out / "result.json").write_text(json.dumps(res, indent=2) + "\n")
    return res


BASE_KEYS = ("verdict", "deciding", "seconds", "runs", "runs_passed", "pass_rate", "stddev", "time", "tokens", "cost_usd")


def mean(res: Result, k: str) -> float | None:
    """Config result RES's mean of K: pass_rate itself, else K's spread mean (None when not measured)."""
    v = res.get(k)
    v = cast("Result", v).get("mean") if isinstance(v, dict) else v
    return float(v) if isinstance(v, int | float) else None


def diff(cur: Result, base: Result, k: str) -> float | None:
    """Current minus baseline mean of K (skill-creator's delta), None when either side has none."""
    c, b = mean(cur, k), mean(base, k)
    return None if c is None or b is None else round(c - b, 4)


def aggregate(done: list[tuple[str, Result]], out: Path, runs: int) -> Result:
    """One config's runs of a case as its result: one run's own, else the first failed run's (or run 1's) with the
    case's verdict and deciding; with runs, runs_passed, pass_rate, stddev, time, tokens and cost_usd."""
    rs = [r for _, r in done]
    ok = [float(r["verdict"] == "PASS") for r in rs]
    use = [run_usage(out / d / "transcript.jsonl") for d, _ in done]
    costs = [cast("float", u["cost_usd"]) for u in use if u["cost_usd"] is not None]
    agg: Result = {"runs": [{"run": k, "dir": d, **{x: r.get(x) for x in RUN_KEYS}, "usage": u, "facts": run_facts(out / d / "grading.json")}
                            for k, ((d, r), u) in enumerate(zip(done, use), 1)],
                   "runs_passed": int(sum(ok)), "pass_rate": round(statistics.fmean(ok), 4),
                   "stddev": round(statistics.stdev(ok), 4) if len(ok) > 1 else 0.0,
                   "time": spread([cast("float", r["seconds"]) for r in rs]),
                   "tokens": spread([cast("float", u["total"]) for u in use]),
                   "cost_usd": spread(costs) if len(costs) == len(use) else None}
    if len(rs) == 1 and done[0][0] == ".":
        return {**rs[0], **agg}

    def said(r: Result) -> str:
        return "; ".join(cast("list[str]", r["deciding"]))

    lead = next((r for r in rs if r["verdict"] == "FAIL"), None) or next((r for r in rs if r["verdict"] != "PASS"), rs[0])   # the first failed run, else run 1
    head = f"{agg['runs_passed']}/{runs} runs passed (pass rate {agg['pass_rate']:.2f}, stddev {agg['stddev']:.2f})"
    why = [f"run {k}: {said(r)}" for k, r in enumerate(rs, 1) if r["verdict"] != "PASS"] or [f"run 1: {said(rs[0])}"]
    secs = round(sum(cast("float", r["seconds"]) for r in rs), 1)
    return {**{k: v for k, v in lead.items() if k not in ("run", "of", "config")}, "verdict": next((v for v in ("FAIL", "REVIEW") if v in {r["verdict"] for r in rs}), "PASS"),
            "deciding": [head, *why], "seconds": secs, **agg}


def show_spread(sp: object, fmt: str = "{:.2f}") -> str:
    if not isinstance(sp, dict) or cast("Result", sp).get("mean") is None:
        return "n/a"
    sp = cast("Result", sp)
    return f"{fmt.format(sp['mean'])} +/- {fmt.format(sp['stddev'])}"


def compare(suite: Result, case: Result, base: Result, cur: Result, configs: list[Config]) -> list[str]:
    """A case's `compare` table (--baseline: --help)."""
    rows = [("pass rate", "pass_rate", "{:.2f}"), ("time s", "time", "{:.1f}"), ("tokens", "tokens", "{:.0f}"), ("cost usd", "cost_usd", "{:.4f}")]
    delta = cast("Result", cur["delta"])
    out = [f"  compare {suite['suite']}/{case['id']}: baseline kit {str(configs[0][3])[:12]} beside current kit {str(configs[-1][3])[:12]}",
           f"    {'':<10} {'baseline':<20} {'current':<20} difference"]

    def shown(res: Result, k: str, fmt: str) -> str:
        return show_spread({"mean": res["pass_rate"], "stddev": res["stddev"]} if k == "pass_rate" else res[k], fmt)

    for lb, k, fmt in rows:
        d = delta[k]
        out.append(f"    {lb:<10} {shown(base, k, fmt):<20} {shown(cur, k, fmt):<20} "
                   + ("n/a" if d is None else ("+" if cast("float", d) >= 0 else "") + fmt.format(d)))
    return out


# ---- a judgment bench -----------------------------------------------------------------------

BENCH_INPUT = "bench-input.json"
BENCH_EXT = "bench-extension.js"
BENCH_COMMAND = "octo-feather-bench"
BUCKETS = (0.0, 0.5, 0.6, 0.7, 0.8, 0.9, 1.0)   # ECE's buckets (schema, Bench), also the confidence table's
Z = 1.96   # the proposed threshold's z (schema, Bench)
JUDGMENT = "model judgment (classifier output, advisory: no gate reads it)"
# The bench as a Pi extension command, run by `pi -e <this> -p "/octo-feather-bench <input path>"`: no agent, no chat
# model. Who answers, on what, and which ids are skipped: schema, Bench; INP skip lists the skipped ids. At most
# 4 calls at once. One
# stdout line {"bench": {available, benched, skipped, errors, rows, calls}}, rows [model, case, choice, probabilities in label
# order, cost, error index]; calls one {model, input_tokens, output_tokens, cost_usd, at} per reg.classify call, the
# usage Pi reported for it (tokens unreported: 0; cost: spec spend#rule-cost), its ledger line (record_spend).
BENCH_SOURCE = """import { readFileSync, writeSync } from "node:fs";
export default function (pi) {
  pi.registerCommand("%(command)s", {
    description: "octo-feather-qa judgment bench: every classifier answers the closed question for each case",
    handler: async (args, ctx) => {
      const inp = JSON.parse(readFileSync(args.trim(), "utf8"));
      const reg = ctx.modelRegistry;
      const all = await reg.getAvailableOfType("classifier");
      const name = (m) => m.provider + "/" + m.id;
      const listed = inp.classifiers ? all.filter((m) => inp.classifiers.includes(name(m))) : all;
      // inp.skip: the ruled-out ids (schema.md, Bench). Without inp.skip (`octo-feather-lane judge`, asking the kit's
      // model): none.
      const skip = inp.skip || [];
      const ruled_out = (m) => skip.includes(name(m));
      const ms = listed.filter((m) => !ruled_out(m));
      const skipped = listed.filter(ruled_out).map(name);
      const q = {type: "choice", instructions: inp.question, criteria: inp.criteria};
      const errors = [];
      const err = (e) => { const s = String(e); if (!errors.includes(s)) errors.push(s); return errors.indexOf(s); };
      const r4 = (x) => (typeof x === "number" ? Math.round(x * 1e4) / 1e4 : null);
      const calls = [];
      const tokens = (x) => (Number.isInteger(x) && x >= 0 ? x : 0);
      const one = async (mi, ci) => {
        let r;
        try { r = await reg.classify(ms[mi], {state: inp.cases[ci].state, questions: {q}}); }
        catch (e) { calls.push({model: name(ms[mi]), input_tokens: 0, output_tokens: 0, cost_usd: null, at: new Date().toISOString()});
                    return [mi, ci, null, null, null, err(e)]; }
        const a = r && r.answers ? r.answers.q : undefined;
        const cost = r && r.usage && r.usage.cost && typeof r.usage.cost.total === "number" ? r.usage.cost.total : null;
        const u = (r && r.usage) || {};
        calls.push({model: name(ms[mi]), input_tokens: tokens(u.input), output_tokens: tokens(u.output), cost_usd: cost,
                    at: new Date().toISOString()});
        if (!r || r.stopReason !== "stop" || !a) return [mi, ci, null, null, cost, err((r && (r.errorMessage || r.stopReason)) || "no result")];
        return [mi, ci, a.choice, inp.labels.map((l) => r4((a.probabilities || {})[l])), cost, null];
      };
      const jobs = [];
      ms.forEach((m, mi) => inp.cases.forEach((c, ci) => jobs.push([mi, ci])));
      const all_rows = new Array(jobs.length);
      let next = 0;
      const lane = async () => { while (next < jobs.length) { const k = next++; all_rows[k] = await one(...jobs[k]); } };
      await Promise.all([lane(), lane(), lane(), lane()]);
      const rows = all_rows;
      const used = [...new Set(rows.map((r) => r[5]).filter((e) => e !== null))];
      const errs = used.map((e) => errors[e]);
      rows.forEach((r) => { if (r[5] !== null) r[5] = used.indexOf(r[5]); });
      const bench = {available: all.map(name), benched: ms.map(name), skipped, errors: errs, rows, calls};
      // Pi keeps stdout for itself in print mode (an extension's process.stdout goes to stderr): write fd 1 directly.
      const buf = Buffer.from(JSON.stringify({bench}) + "\\n");
      const nap = new Int32Array(new SharedArrayBuffer(4));
      for (let off = 0; off < buf.length;) {
        try { off += writeSync(1, buf, off); }
        catch (e) { if (e.code !== "EAGAIN") throw e; Atomics.wait(nap, 0, 0, 10); }
      }
    },
  });
}
"""


def bench_output(stdout):
    """(bench, problem): the command's one {"bench": ...} stdout line; problem names why there is none."""
    for t in stdout.splitlines():
        o = safe_json(t)
        if isinstance(o, dict) and isinstance(o.get("bench"), dict):
            return o["bench"], None
    return None, "the bench command printed no bench result: " + stdout[-300:].replace("\n", " ")


def calibration(answered, labels):
    """Brier and ECE (rule: schema, Bench), the buckets [lo, hi, n, mean top probability, accuracy], and each case's Brier term."""
    terms, tops = [], []
    for a in answered:
        ps = [p if isinstance(p, (int, float)) else 0.0 for p in a["probabilities"]]
        s = sum(ps) or 1.0
        ps = [p / s for p in ps]
        terms.append(sum((p - (lb == a["label"])) ** 2 for p, lb in zip(ps, labels)))
        tops.append((max(ps), a["choice"] == a["label"]))
    buckets = []
    for lo, hi in zip(BUCKETS, BUCKETS[1:]):
        inb = [(p, ok) for p, ok in tops if lo <= p < hi or (hi == 1.0 and p == 1.0)]
        if inb:
            buckets.append([lo, hi, len(inb), sum(p for p, _ in inb) / len(inb), sum(ok for _, ok in inb) / len(inb)])
    n = len(tops)
    return {"brier": sum(terms) / n if n else None, "ece": sum(b[2] / n * abs(b[4] - b[3]) for b in buckets) if n else None,
            "buckets": buckets, "_terms": terms}


def split_metrics(rows, labels):
    answered = [r for r in rows if r["choice"] in labels]
    correct = sum(r["choice"] == r["label"] for r in answered)
    return {"cases": len(rows), "answered": len(answered), "correct": correct,
            "accuracy": correct / len(answered) if answered else None, **calibration(answered, labels)}


def wilson_low(k, n):
    if not n:
        return None
    p = k / n
    return (p + Z * Z / (2 * n) - Z * ((p * (1 - p) + Z * Z / (4 * n)) / n) ** 0.5) / (1 + Z * Z / n)


MODEL_FILE = "judgment-model.json"   # in the evals dir (schema, Judgment model and classifiers)
BEST_RULE = "highest train accuracy over every train case answered; ties: lower train Brier, lower train cost, name"


CLASSIFIERS = "classifiers.json"   # in the evals dir (schema: .agents/skills/eval-cases/references/schema.md, Judgment model and classifiers)


def classifier_lists(evals):
    """EVALS/classifiers.json, parsed (its schema: the eval-cases skill, Judgment model and classifiers)."""
    return json.loads((Path(evals) / CLASSIFIERS).read_text())


def unclassified_ids(bench, ruled):
    """The benched classifiers in no list of classifiers.json (rule: schema, Bench, Classes)."""
    return [m for m in bench.get("benched") or [] if m not in ruled["pinned"]]


def yes_no_skipped(bench, ruled):
    """The skipped classifiers classifiers.json lists yes/no only, each with its entry (its keys: schema, Judgment model and classifiers)."""
    return {m: ruled["yes_no_only"][m] for m in bench.get("skipped") or [] if m in ruled["yes_no_only"]}


def judgment_model(evals):
    """The kit's one judgment model, P/ID, from EVALS/judgment-model.json (its schema: the eval-cases skill, Judgment model and classifiers)."""
    return json.loads((Path(evals) / MODEL_FILE).read_text())["model"]


def bench_metrics(bench, cases, labels, kit_model=None, ruled=None):
    """Per benched model: scores per split; the question's best-scoring classifier and the kit's model's proposed
    threshold (rules: schema, Bench)."""
    errors = bench.get("errors") or []
    names = bench.get("benched") or []
    per = {m: [] for m in names}
    answers = []
    for mi, ci, choice, probs, cost, ei in bench.get("rows") or []:
        c, e = cases[ci]
        row = {"model": names[mi], "case": c["id"], "split": c["split"], "label": e["label"], "choice": choice,
               "probabilities": probs, "cost": cost, "error": errors[ei] if ei is not None else None, "judgment": JUDGMENT}
        per[names[mi]].append(row); answers.append(row)
    models = []
    for m in names:
        rows = per[m]
        sp = {s: split_metrics([r for r in rows if r["split"] == s], labels) for s in ("train", "held-out")}
        errs = [r["error"] or f"answer {r['choice']!r} not a label" for r in rows if r["choice"] not in labels]
        costs = [r["cost"] for r in rows if r["cost"] is not None]
        models.append({"model": m, "train": sp["train"], "held-out": sp["held-out"], "cost_usd": sum(costs),
                       "train_cost_usd": sum(r["cost"] for r in rows if r["cost"] is not None and r["split"] == "train"),
                       "cost_unreported": len(rows) - len(costs), "errors": len(errs), "first_error": errs[0] if errs else None,
                       "available": any(r["choice"] in labels for r in rows)})
    n_train = sum(c["split"] == "train" for c, _ in cases)
    eligible = [m for m in models if n_train and m["train"]["answered"] == n_train]
    eligible.sort(key=lambda m: (-m["train"]["accuracy"], m["train"]["brier"], m["train_cost_usd"], m["model"]))
    best = {"model": eligible[0]["model"], "rule": BEST_RULE} if eligible else None
    kit = None
    if kit_model is not None:
        c = next((m for m in eligible if m["model"] == kit_model), None)
        kit = {"model": kit_model, "scored": c is not None}
        if c is None:
            k = next((m for m in models if m["model"] == kit_model), None)
            kit["why"] = ((("yes/no only" if kit_model in (ruled or {}).get("yes_no_only", {}) else "a moving alias")
                           if kit_model in (bench.get("skipped") or [])
                           else "not benched") if k is None else f"answered {k['train']['answered']} of {n_train} train cases"
                          + (f", first error: {k['first_error']}" if k["first_error"] else ""))
        else:
            t = c["train"]["_terms"]; n = len(t); mean = sum(t) / n
            sd = (sum((x - mean) ** 2 for x in t) / (n - 1)) ** 0.5 if n > 1 else 0.0
            thr = {"accuracy_min": round(wilson_low(c["train"]["correct"], n), 3), "brier_max": round(mean + Z * sd / n ** 0.5, 3)}
            h = c["held-out"]
            meets = (h["answered"] == h["cases"] and h["answered"] > 0 and h["accuracy"] >= thr["accuracy_min"]
                     and h["brier"] <= thr["brier_max"])
            kit.update(threshold=thr, threshold_rule=f"from train only: accuracy_min the Wilson {Z} lower bound of train "
                       f"accuracy, brier_max train Brier mean + {Z} standard errors", held_out_meets=meets,
                       held_out={"accuracy": None if h["accuracy"] is None else round(h["accuracy"], 3),
                                 "brier": None if h["brier"] is None else round(h["brier"], 3)})
    for m in models:
        for s in ("train", "held-out"):
            m[s].pop("_terms", None)
    return models, best, kit, answers


def span(lo, hi):
    return f"[{lo}, {hi}" + ("]" if hi == BUCKETS[-1] else ")")


def bench_report(suite, q, cases, bench, models, best, kit, requested, ruled):
    f = lambda x, d=3: "-" if x is None else f"{x:.{d}f}"
    n = {s: sum(c["split"] == s for c, _ in cases) for s in ("train", "held-out")}
    out = [f"bench {suite['suite']}: question {q['id']}, labels {', '.join(q['labels'])}; {len(cases)} cases (train {n['train']}, "
           f"held-out {n['held-out']}); every answer is a {JUDGMENT}",
           f"bench {suite['suite']}: classifiers available ({len(bench.get('available') or [])}): {', '.join(bench.get('available') or []) or 'none'}"]
    if requested:
        miss = [m for m in requested if m not in (bench.get("benched") or []) + (bench.get("skipped") or [])]
        out.append(f"bench {suite['suite']}: benched only --classifier {', '.join(requested)}" + (f" (not available: {', '.join(miss)})" if miss else ""))
    moving = [m for m in bench.get("skipped") or [] if m in ruled["moving_alias"]]
    if moving:
        out.append(f"bench {suite['suite']}: skipped: moving alias ({len(moving)}): {', '.join(moving)}; never "
                   f"called, ruling ({CLASSIFIERS} owner): {ruled['owner']}")
    for m, y in yes_no_skipped(bench, ruled).items():
        out.append(f"bench {suite['suite']}: skipped: yes/no only {m}; never called, ruling ({CLASSIFIERS} yes_no_only): "
                   f"{y['ruling']}; provider error ({y['evidence']}): {y['error']}")
    unclassified = unclassified_ids(bench, ruled)
    if unclassified:
        out.append(f"bench {suite['suite']}: unclassified id ({len(unclassified)}): {', '.join(unclassified)}; benched (scored where it answered), "
                   f"in no list of {CLASSIFIERS}, never the kit's model until the owner rules it there")
    ok = sorted((m for m in models if m["available"]), key=lambda m: (-(m["train"]["accuracy"] or 0), m["train"]["brier"] or 9, m["model"]))
    w = max([len(m["model"]) for m in models] + [5])
    for s, what in (("train", "the best and the kit model's threshold are made here"), ("held-out", "the measure, never used to pick")):
        out.append(f"{s.upper()} ({n[s]} cases; {what}):")
        out.append(f"  {'model':<{w}}  answered  correct  accuracy  brier   ece     cost_usd   errors")
        for m in ok:
            x = m[s]
            out.append(f"  {m['model']:<{w}}  {x['answered']:>3}/{x['cases']:<4}  {x['correct']:>7}  {f(x['accuracy']):>8}  {f(x['brier']):<6}  "
                       f"{f(x['ece']):<6}  {f(m['cost_usd'], 6):>9}  {m['errors']}")
    out.append("  (cost_usd and errors: the model's every call, train and held-out; brier: mean multi-class Brier score, lower is "
               "better; ece: expected calibration error over top-probability buckets " + ", ".join(span(a, b) for a, b in zip(BUCKETS, BUCKETS[1:])) + ")")
    for m in models:
        if not m["available"]:
            out.append(f"unavailable {m['model']}: listed but answered no case: {m['first_error']}")
        elif m["errors"]:
            out.append(f"errors {m['model']}: {m['errors']} case(s) unanswered, first: {m['first_error']}")
    out.append(f"KIT MODEL BESIDE THE BEST (best: {BEST_RULE}; held-out apart, never used to pick):")
    out.append(f"  {'':<4}  {'model':<{w}}  train acc  train brier  held-out acc  held-out brier  cost_usd")
    for role, name in (("kit", kit and kit["model"]), ("best", best and best["model"])):
        m = next((m for m in models if m["model"] == name and m["available"]), None)
        if m is None:
            out.append(f"  {role:<4}  {name or 'none':<{w}}  " + ("not scored: " + kit["why"] if role == "kit" and kit else
                                                                "no classifier answered every train case"))
            continue
        out.append(f"  {role:<4}  {m['model']:<{w}}  {f(m['train']['accuracy']):>9}  {f(m['train']['brier']):>11}  "
                   f"{f(m['held-out']['accuracy']):>12}  {f(m['held-out']['brier']):>14}  {f(m['cost_usd'], 6):>8}")
    if kit and kit["scored"]:
        c = next(m for m in models if m["model"] == kit["model"]); t = kit["threshold"]; h = c["held-out"]
        out.append(f"kit model {kit['model']} (" + MODEL_FILE + f"): proposed threshold (for the director to accept; until met, "
                   f"the judge stays advisory): held-out accuracy >= {t['accuracy_min']} and held-out brier <= {t['brier_max']} "
                   f"({kit['threshold_rule']})")
        out.append(f"held-out now: accuracy {f(h['accuracy'])} ({h['correct']}/{h['answered']} of {h['cases']}), brier {f(h['brier'])}, "
                   f"ece {f(h['ece'])}: {'meets' if kit['held_out_meets'] else 'does not meet'} the proposed threshold")
        for s in ("train", "held-out"):
            out.append(f"kit model calibration {s} (top probability bucket: n, mean top probability, accuracy): " + ("; ".join(
                f"{span(b[0], b[1])} n {b[2]} p {b[3]:.3f} acc {b[4]:.3f}" for b in c[s]["buckets"]) or "no answers"))
    return out


def run_bench(qc, d, suite, picked, requested, runid, out, kit_model):
    """One judgment suite's bench: pi in the qa sandbox runs the BENCH_SOURCE extension's command (no agent), every
    available classifier answers each picked case's state; graded here against reference/expectations.json, never shown to it."""
    out.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)
    q = json.loads((d / "question.json").read_text())
    tmo = int(suite.get("timeout_s", DEFAULT_TIMEOUT))
    t0 = time.time()
    res = {"suite": suite["suite"], "kind": "judgment", "question": q["id"], "cases": len(picked)}
    ruled = classifier_lists(d.parent)
    inp = {"question": q["question"], "labels": q["labels"], "criteria": {lb: q["label_help"][lb] for lb in q["labels"]},
           "cases": [{"id": c["id"], "state": c["state"]} for c, _ in picked], "classifiers": requested or None,
           "skip": ruled["moving_alias"] + list(ruled["yes_no_only"])}
    bench, run, rec, problem = classify(qc, inp, tmo, f"qa-{runid}-bench", out, purpose="bench")
    res["seconds"] = round(time.time() - t0, 1)
    if problem:
        return bench_end(out, res, problem)
    models, best, kit, answers = bench_metrics(bench, picked, q["labels"], kit_model, ruled)
    (out / "answers.json").write_text(json.dumps({"judgment": JUDGMENT, "answers": answers}, indent=1) + "\n")
    lines = bench_report(suite, q, picked, bench, models, best, kit, requested, ruled)
    (out / "report.txt").write_text("\n".join(lines) + "\n")
    print("\n".join(lines), flush=True)
    res.update(available=bench.get("available"), benched=bench.get("benched"), skipped=bench.get("skipped") or [],
               skipped_ruling=ruled["owner"] if set(bench.get("skipped") or []) & set(ruled["moving_alias"]) else None,
               skipped_yes_no_only=yes_no_skipped(bench, ruled),
               unclassified=unclassified_ids(bench, ruled),
               models=models, best=best, kit_model=kit, cost_usd=sum(m["cost_usd"] for m in models))
    asked = not requested or kit_model in requested   # --classifier without the kit's model (schema, Bench: when a bench FAILS)
    problem = ("no classifier answered every train case" if not best else
               f"the kit's judgment model {kit_model} was not scored ({kit['why']})" if asked and not kit["scored"] else None)
    return bench_end(out, res, problem)


def classify(qc, inp, tmo, session, out=None, *, purpose):
    """The one classify path, the bench's and `octo-feather-lane judge`'s: pi in the qa sandbox (session SESSION, no lane
    history, offline gh off) runs the BENCH_SOURCE extension's command on INP ({question, labels, criteria: {label: help},
    cases: [{id, state}], classifiers: [P/ID] or None}), no agent, within TMO seconds. Returns (bench, run, sandbox record,
    problem): bench the command's {available, benched, skipped, errors, rows, calls}, None with problem naming why. With OUT,
    writes input.json, extension.js, sandbox.json, stdout.txt and stderr.txt there. Then records each of its calls under
    PURPOSE in the spend ledger (record_spend)."""
    scratch = Path(tempfile.mkdtemp(prefix=f"{session}-"))
    try:
        (scratch / BENCH_INPUT).write_text(json.dumps(inp, indent=1) + "\n")
        ext = BENCH_SOURCE % {"command": BENCH_COMMAND}
        (scratch / BENCH_EXT).write_text(ext)
        g = ["git", "-C", str(scratch), "-c", "user.name=octo-feather-qa", "-c", "user.email=qa@octo-feather.invalid",
             "-c", "commit.gpgsign=false", "-c", "core.hooksPath=/dev/null"]
        for a in (["init", "-q", "-b", "main"], ["add", "-A"], ["commit", "-qm", "bench input"]):
            subprocess.run([*g, *a], check=True, capture_output=True)
        if out:
            (out / "input.json").write_text(json.dumps(inp, indent=2) + "\n")
            (out / "extension.js").write_text(ext)
        cmd = ["timeout", "-k", "10", str(tmo), "pi", "--no-session", "--no-skills", "--no-mcp", "--no-context-files",
               "--no-prompt-templates", "--no-extensions", "--no-tools", "-e", str(scratch / BENCH_EXT),
               "-p", f"/{BENCH_COMMAND} {scratch / BENCH_INPUT}"]
        here = os.getcwd(); os.chdir(scratch)
        try:
            run, rec = qc.sandboxed(cmd, session, {"off": GH_OFF}, history=False)
        except SystemExit as e:
            run, rec = None, {"error": f"sandbox unavailable (exit {e.code})"}
        finally:
            os.chdir(here)
    finally:
        shutil.rmtree(scratch, ignore_errors=True)
    if out:
        (out / "sandbox.json").write_text(json.dumps(rec, indent=2) + "\n")
    if run is None:
        bad = [l for l in rec.get("proof", []) if "FAIL" in l] or [rec.get("error", "sandbox did not start")]
        return None, None, rec, f"sandbox: proof failed, bench not run: {'; '.join(bad)}"
    if out:
        (out / "stdout.txt").write_text(run.stdout)
        (out / "stderr.txt").write_text(run.stderr)
    bench, problem = bench_output(run.stdout)
    if bench is not None:
        record_spend(qc, bench.get("calls") or [], purpose)
    return bench, run, rec, (f"{problem} (pi exit {run.returncode})" if problem else None)


def record_spend(qc, calls, purpose):
    """CALLS (the bench command's), one ledger line each under PURPOSE, recorded as octo-feather-qc record_spend says
    (spec spend, writer-bench and writer-judge rows)."""
    qc.record_spend([json.dumps({**c, "purpose": purpose}) for c in calls], purpose)


def bench_end(out, res, problem):
    res["verdict"] = "FAILED" if problem else "DONE"
    if problem:
        res["problem"] = problem
    (out / "bench.json").write_text(json.dumps(res, indent=2) + "\n")
    k = res.get("kit_model") or {}
    said = problem or (f"kit model {k['model']}" + ("" if k.get("scored") else f" not scored ({k.get('why')})")
                       + f", best {res['best']['model']}")
    print(f"{res['verdict']} bench {res['suite']}: {said} [{res['seconds']} s]", flush=True)
    return res


# ---- main -----------------------------------------------------------------------------------

def gate_free():
    p = subprocess.run([str(KIT / "scripts" / "check-gate-free"), "--refuse", "the factory evals (octo-feather-qa)"],
                       stdout=subprocess.PIPE, text=True)
    if p.stdout.strip() != "gate-free: ok":
        die(70, "refused inside just check, which stays deterministic and free (message above)")


SLOT: list[subprocess.Popen[str]] = []   # the eval slot's hold, kept for this run's life


def eval_slot():
    """The eval slot (octo-feather-slot --help): held until this process exits, or the run refused, nothing run."""
    p = subprocess.Popen([str(KIT / "scripts" / "octo-feather-slot"), "hold", "--kind", "eval"],
                         stdin=subprocess.PIPE, stdout=subprocess.PIPE, text=True)
    SLOT.append(p)
    said = p.stdout.readline().rstrip("\n") if p.stdout else ""
    if said.startswith(("held:", "free:", "nested:")):
        print(f"qa: eval slot: {said}", flush=True)
        return
    print((said + (p.stdout.read() if p.stdout else "")).rstrip("\n"), file=sys.stderr)
    sys.exit(p.wait() or 75)


def parse(argv):
    opts = {"suite": [], "case": [], "classifier": [], "model": None, "evals": None, "sample": None, "runs": None, "kit-ref": None, "baseline": None}
    it = iter(argv)
    for a in it:
        if a in ("-h", "--help"):
            print(__doc__.strip()); sys.exit(0)
        k = a[2:] if a in ("--suite", "--case", "--classifier", "--model", "--evals", "--sample", "--runs", "--kit-ref", "--baseline") else None
        if k is None:
            die(64, f"unknown argument {a!r} (see --help)")
        v = next(it, None)
        if v is None:
            die(64, f"{a} needs a value")
        if isinstance(opts[k], list):
            opts[k].append(v)
        else:
            opts[k] = v
    if opts["sample"] is not None and not (opts["sample"].isdigit() and int(opts["sample"]) > 0):
        die(64, f"--sample needs a positive integer, got {opts['sample']!r}")
    r = cast("str | None", opts["runs"])
    if isinstance(r, str) and not (r.isdigit() and int(r) > 0):
        die(64, f"--runs needs a positive integer, got {r!r}")
    return opts


def stratum(case):
    return case.get("should_trigger"), case.get("split")


def sample(picked, n):
    """n of picked, stratified by (should_trigger, split): each stratum shuffled with a fixed seed, then one
    from each in turn; should_trigger true/train and false/held-out lead, so 2 picks hold one of each."""
    rng = random.Random(SAMPLE_SEED)
    strata = {}
    for p in picked:
        strata.setdefault(stratum(p[1]), []).append(p)
    keys = sorted(strata, key=lambda k: (k[0] != (k[1] == "train"), str(k)))
    pools = []
    for k in keys:
        pool = sorted(strata[k], key=lambda p: (p[0]["suite"], p[1]["id"]))
        rng.shuffle(pool)
        pools.append(pool)
    chosen = []
    while len(chosen) < n and any(pools):
        for pool in pools:
            if pool and len(chosen) < n:
                chosen.append(id(pool.pop(0)))
    return [p for p in picked if id(p) in chosen]


def scores(results):
    """{split: {passed, total}} over the cases that have a split; {} when none has one."""
    if not any("split" in r for r in results):
        return {}
    return {sp: {"passed": sum(r["verdict"] == "PASS" for r in results if r.get("split") == sp),
                 "total": sum(r.get("split") == sp for r in results)} for sp in ("train", "held-out")}


TRADEOFF = 0.5   # a cost tradeoff's growth over the baseline mean (rule: --help, --analyze)


def analyze(cases: list[Result]) -> Result:
    """The deterministic analysis of a run's fact cases (rules: --help, --analyze); no model."""
    nd_cases: list[Result] = []
    nd_facts: list[Result] = []
    hv: list[Result] = []
    cost: list[Result] = []
    for r in cases:
        if "runs" not in r or "review" in r:
            continue
        name = f"{r['suite']}/{r['id']}"
        b = r.get("baseline")
        base = cast("Result", b) if isinstance(b, dict) else None
        for kit, x in ([("baseline", base), ("current", r)] if base else [("", r)]):
            if 0 < cast("float", x["pass_rate"]) < 1:
                hv.append({"case": name, "kit": kit or None, "pass_rate": x["pass_rate"], "stddev": x["stddev"]})
        if base is None:
            continue
        same = r["pass_rate"] == base["pass_rate"]
        grew: Result = {}
        for k in ("time", "tokens"):
            c, bm = mean(r, k), mean(base, k)
            if c is not None and bm is not None and c > bm * (1 + TRADEOFF):
                grew[k] = {"baseline": bm, "current": c}
        if same and grew:
            cost.append({"case": name, "pass_rate": r["pass_rate"], **grew})
        elif same and r["pass_rate"] in (0.0, 1.0):
            nd_cases.append({"case": name, "pass_rate": r["pass_rate"]})
        if not same:
            fl = [cast("list[Result]", cast("Result", x).get("facts") or []) for x in cast("list[object]", base["runs"]) + cast("list[object]", r["runs"])]
            for i in range(min(len(f) for f in fl) if fl else 0):
                st = {f[i].get("status") for f in fl}
                if len(st) == 1:
                    nd_facts.append({"case": name, "fact": {k: v for k, v in fl[0][i].items() if k != "status"}, "status": st.pop()})
    return {"threshold": TRADEOFF, "non_discriminating_cases": nd_cases, "non_discriminating_facts": nd_facts,
            "high_variance": hv, "cost_tradeoffs": cost}


def analysis_lines(a: Result) -> list[str]:
    """The analysis as printed: one line per flag, or `no flags`."""
    def fact(f: Result) -> str:
        return " ".join([str(f.get("fact")), *(json.dumps(v) if isinstance(v, list | dict) else str(v) for k, v in f.items() if k != "fact")])

    out = ["qa: analysis (deterministic, no model; rules: octo-feather-qa --help, --analyze):"]
    out += [f"  non-discriminating case {x['case']}: every run on both kits {'passed' if x['pass_rate'] == 1.0 else 'failed'}"
            for x in cast("list[Result]", a["non_discriminating_cases"])]
    out += [f"  non-discriminating fact {x['case']}: {fact(cast('Result', x['fact']))}: {x['status']} in every run on both kits"
            for x in cast("list[Result]", a["non_discriminating_facts"])]
    out += [f"  high variance {x['case']}: " + (f"{x['kit']} kit " if x["kit"] else "") + f"pass rate {x['pass_rate']:.2f} +/- {x['stddev']:.2f}"
            for x in cast("list[Result]", a["high_variance"])]
    out += [f"  cost tradeoff {x['case']}: pass rate {x['pass_rate']:.2f} on both kits; " + "; ".join(
            f"{k} mean {cast('Result', x[k])['baseline']:.1f} to {cast('Result', x[k])['current']:.1f}" for k in ("time", "tokens") if k in x)
            for x in cast("list[Result]", a["cost_tradeoffs"])]
    return out if len(out) > 1 else [*out, "  no flags"]


def reanalyze(run_dir: str) -> int:
    """--analyze RUN_DIR: the analysis of a stored run, from its summary.json only; no case, sandbox or model runs."""
    p = Path(run_dir) / "summary.json"
    try:
        raw: object = json.loads(p.read_text())
    except (OSError, ValueError) as e:
        raw = f"no readable summary.json ({e})"
    if not isinstance(raw, dict):
        die(64, f"--analyze {run_dir}: {raw if isinstance(raw, str) else 'summary.json is not an object'}")
    sm = cast("Result", raw)
    print(f"qa: run {sm.get('run_id')} reanalyzed from {p}", flush=True)
    print("\n".join(analysis_lines(analyze(cast("list[Result]", sm.get("cases") or [])))), flush=True)
    return 0


def main(argv: list[str]):
    if argv[:1] == ["--watch"]:
        return watch(argv[1:])
    if argv[:1] == ["--review"]:
        return review(argv[1:])
    if argv[:1] == ["--analyze"]:
        if argv[2:] or not argv[1:]:
            die(64, "--analyze takes one RUN_DIR and no other option")
        return reanalyze(argv[1])
    gate_free()
    o = parse(argv)
    eval_slot()
    evals = Path(o["evals"]).resolve() if o["evals"] else KIT / "evals"
    chk = subprocess.run([str(KIT / "scripts" / "check-evals"), str(evals)])
    if chk.returncode:
        die(2, "eval cases are malformed (check-evals, above); nothing run")
    suites = {}
    for d in sorted(p for p in evals.iterdir() if p.is_dir() and p.name != "fixtures"):
        s = json.loads((d / "suite.json").read_text())
        suites[d.name] = (s, json.loads((d / "cases.json").read_text()), json.loads((d / "reference" / "expectations.json").read_text()))
    unknown = [s for s in o["suite"] if s not in suites]
    if unknown:
        die(64, f"no suite {' '.join(unknown)} in {evals} (have: {' '.join(suites) or 'none'})")
    picked = [(s, c, e[c["id"]] if s["kind"] == "judgment" else e[c["id"]]["facts"]) for name, (s, cs, e) in suites.items()
              if not o["suite"] or name in o["suite"] for c in cs if not o["case"] or c["id"] in o["case"]]
    unknown = [c for c in o["case"] if c not in {c["id"] for _, c, _ in picked}]
    if unknown:
        die(64, f"no case {' '.join(unknown)} in the selected suites")
    if not picked:
        die(64, "no cases selected")
    if o["sample"]:
        total = len(picked)
        picked = sample(picked, int(o["sample"]))
        show_case = lambda c: f"{c['id']} (should_trigger {str(c.get('should_trigger')).lower()}, {c.get('split', 'no split')})"
        print(f"qa: sample {len(picked)} of {total} (seed {SAMPLE_SEED!r}, stratified by should_trigger and split): "
              + ", ".join(f"{s['suite']}/{show_case(c)}" for s, c, _ in picked), flush=True)
    kit, sha = kit_at(o["kit-ref"])
    base: tuple[Path, str | None] | None = None
    # mise's state dir one per qa run, removed after it: a mise shim (uv) run in a case repo outside the sandbox
    # (fixture setup, the sandbox's setup before its own per-run dir) records the repo's mise.toml there, never in
    # the caller's, where the link dangles once the scratch goes (#664).
    ms = tempfile.mkdtemp(prefix="qa-mise-state-")
    os.environ["MISE_STATE_DIR"] = ms
    try:
        base = kit_at(o["baseline"], "--baseline") if o["baseline"] else None
        return run_all(o, evals, picked, kit, sha, base)
    finally:
        shutil.rmtree(ms, ignore_errors=True)
        for k in (kit, base[0] if base else KIT):
            if k != KIT:
                shutil.rmtree(k, ignore_errors=True)


def run_all(o, evals, picked, kit, sha, base: "tuple[Path, str | None] | None" = None):
    runid = f"{time.strftime('%Y%m%dT%H%M%SZ', time.gmtime())}-{secrets.token_hex(3)}"
    root = Path(os.environ.get("OCTO_FEATHER_QA_DIR") or Path(subprocess.run(
        [str(KIT / "scripts" / "octo-feather-state")], capture_output=True, text=True).stdout.strip()) / "qa")
    run_dir = root / runid; run_dir.mkdir(parents=True)
    REVIEWS[:] = [root / "reviews"]
    runs = int(cast("str | None", o["runs"]) or "1")
    print(f"qa: run {runid}: {len(picked)} case(s)" + (f", {runs} runs each" if runs > 1 else "") + f"; kit {sha}" + (f" (--kit-ref {o['kit-ref']})" if o["kit-ref"] else "")
          + (f"; baseline kit {base[1]} (--baseline {o['baseline']}), runs interleaved" if base else "") + f"; artifacts {run_dir}", flush=True)
    qc = qc_sandbox()
    t0 = time.time()
    results = [run_runs(qc, evals, s, c, f, o["model"], runid.split("-")[-1], n, run_dir / s["suite"] / c["id"], runs,
                        [*([("baseline", base[0], o["baseline"], base[1])] if base else []),
                         ("current" if base else "", kit, o["kit-ref"], sha)])
               for n, (s, c, f) in enumerate(picked, 1) if s["kind"] != "judgment"]
    benches = []
    for name in dict.fromkeys(s["suite"] for s, _, _ in picked if s["kind"] == "judgment"):
        s = next(s for s, _, _ in picked if s["suite"] == name)
        benches.append(run_bench(qc, evals / name, s, [(c, e) for x, c, e in picked if x is s], o["classifier"],
                                 runid.split("-")[-1], run_dir / name, judgment_model(evals)))
    passed = sum(r["verdict"] == "PASS" for r in results)
    sc = scores(results)
    an = analyze(results)
    if results and (base or runs > 1):
        print("\n".join(analysis_lines(an)), flush=True)
    for sp, v in sc.items():
        print(f"qa: {sp} score {v['passed']}/{v['total']} passed")
    (run_dir / "summary.json").write_text(json.dumps({"run_id": runid, "kit_ref": o["kit-ref"] or "HEAD", "kit_sha": sha,
                                                      "passed": passed, "total": len(results), "scores": sc, "runs": runs,
                                                      **({"baseline": {"kit_ref": o["baseline"], "kit_sha": base[1]}} if base else {}),
                                                      "seconds": round(time.time() - t0, 1), "cases": results, "analysis": an,
                                                      **({"benches": benches} if benches else {})}, indent=2) + "\n")
    if results:
        print(f"qa: {passed}/{len(results)} passed (run {runid}); artifacts {run_dir}")
    if benches:
        print(f"qa: {sum(b['verdict'] == 'DONE' for b in benches)}/{len(benches)} bench(es) done (run {runid}); artifacts {run_dir}")
    return 0 if passed == len(results) and all(b["verdict"] == "DONE" for b in benches) else 1


if __name__ == "__main__":
    sys.exit(main(sys.argv[1:]))
